1
00:00:00,199 --> 00:00:02,199
(Sound of the pendulum of the wall clock)

2
00:00:03,126 --> 00:00:05,008
The day that Agha Jan and Dear Uncle Napoleon,

3
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:06,161
made peace with each other,

4
00:00:06,186 --> 00:00:08,799
the whole family drew a breath of relief.

5
00:00:09,574 --> 00:00:10,603
But when Agha Jan,

6
00:00:10,627 --> 00:00:12,479
rented his house to an Indian man,

7
00:00:12,871 --> 00:00:14,655
I realized that this reconciliation

8
00:00:14,679 --> 00:00:16,590
is the prelude to a psychological war,

9
00:00:16,615 --> 00:00:17,178
that Agha Jan,

10
00:00:17,202 --> 00:00:19,207
has started to drive Dear Uncle crazy!

11
00:00:20,029 --> 00:00:20,768
Dear Uncle

12
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,086
saw all Indians

13
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:24,010
as English spies,

14
00:00:24,197 --> 00:00:24,878
and Agha Jan,

15
00:00:24,903 --> 00:00:27,654
had rented his own house to an Indian!

16
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:31,208
A few days after Sardar Maharat-Khan moved

17
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:32,147
into our alley,

18
00:00:32,421 --> 00:00:35,158
on August 25, 1941,

19
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:37,226
the Allies attacked Iran.

20
00:00:38,477 --> 00:00:38,992
Dear Uncle,

21
00:00:39,016 --> 00:00:40,252
thinking that the English

22
00:00:40,277 --> 00:00:42,094
had come to arrest him,

23
00:00:42,582 --> 00:00:44,904
after consulting Agha Jan, decided

24
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:47,577
to flee Tehran for Nishapur!

25
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,951
I informed Shazdeh Asdollah-Mirza.

26
00:00:51,376 --> 00:00:53,856
And Shazdeh with the help of Sardar Maharat-Khan,

27
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:55,441
staged a scene so that

28
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,115
so that Dear Uncle Napoleon would give up fleeing.

29
00:00:58,483 --> 00:01:01,941
(Sound of horses trotting)

30
00:01:02,089 --> 00:01:07,073
Dear Uncle Napoleon Episode 8

31
00:01:08,141 --> 00:01:13,081
Based on the novel Dear Uncle Napoleon, written by Iraj Pezeshkzad

32
00:01:13,523 --> 00:01:15,523
(Sound of horses trotting) Subtitles: Iman Soleimani Zadeh

33
00:01:16,499 --> 00:01:18,499
(Sound of gunfire and the murmur of warriors)

34
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:20,134
Stop!

35
00:03:23,093 --> 00:03:24,021
Sir!

36
00:03:29,219 --> 00:03:30,615
Sir! He came toward us!

37
00:03:30,853 --> 00:03:31,868
Oh, good Lord!

38
00:03:32,536 --> 00:03:33,907
Happy journey, Sahib!

39
00:03:34,514 --> 00:03:36,736
We will all be missing you, kartahe!

40
00:03:36,761 --> 00:03:37,711
Thank you very much!

41
00:03:37,736 --> 00:03:40,050
How nice that we saw you, so we could

42
00:03:40,075 --> 00:03:41,075
say goodbye!

43
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,357
It’s been a while since we went on pilgrimage...

44
00:03:43,694 --> 00:03:45,796
to Lady Masoumeh’s shrine!

45
00:03:45,821 --> 00:03:47,005
But you having no fear at all

46
00:03:47,116 --> 00:03:49,534
that the road be unsafe? With all this war and fighting?

47
00:03:49,617 --> 00:03:50,212
Sahib?

48
00:03:50,526 --> 00:03:52,115
No no Sardar!

49
00:03:52,186 --> 00:03:54,422
These words are all rumors!

50
00:03:54,447 --> 00:03:56,841
What does war have to do with us?

51
00:03:56,866 --> 00:03:57,241
- Yes!

52
00:03:57,266 --> 00:03:59,377
Besides, God forbid,

53
00:03:59,402 --> 00:04:01,589
even if something should happen,

54
00:04:01,614 --> 00:04:03,626
Lady Masoumeh herself protects the pilgrims!

55
00:04:03,651 --> 00:04:04,033
Yes!-

56
00:04:04,208 --> 00:04:04,578
Sahib!

57
00:04:04,675 --> 00:04:07,643
Why wife and child with you taking nakartahe?

58
00:04:08,198 --> 00:04:08,970
A few days!

59
00:04:08,995 --> 00:04:11,410
It will not take more than a few days!

60
00:04:11,435 --> 00:04:12,788
Yes! A few days...

61
00:04:12,954 --> 00:04:13,603
Yes.

62
00:04:13,628 --> 00:04:14,584
But Sahib!

63
00:04:14,695 --> 00:04:17,163
Separation, however short,

64
00:04:17,188 --> 00:04:19,330
is very heart-searing...

65
00:04:19,953 --> 00:04:21,342
As the poet says:

66
00:04:21,624 --> 00:04:25,642
My beloved is in Lahore and I am in Nishapur...

67
00:04:25,734 --> 00:04:26,952
M... M... M... Mohammad Aqa!

68
00:04:27,217 --> 00:04:28,035
Get moving!

69
00:04:28,283 --> 00:04:29,614
Qasem don’t look at him!

70
00:04:31,382 --> 00:04:32,164
- Safe travels

71
00:04:32,381 --> 00:04:33,711
Dear Uncle! Don’t forget the souvenir.

72
00:04:33,736 --> 00:04:34,958
- Goodbye, Daddy! - Leili dear, take care!

73
00:04:35,308 --> 00:04:35,810
- Goodbye

74
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:36,157
- Move aside!

75
00:04:36,241 --> 00:04:36,842
- Goodbye

76
00:04:37,049 --> 00:04:38,122
- All the best - Safe travels

77
00:04:38,382 --> 00:04:39,209
- God be with you

78
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:39,976
- Goodbye!

79
00:04:40,001 --> 00:04:41,046
- Goodbye

80
00:04:41,071 --> 00:04:41,882
- Goodbye

81
00:04:42,045 --> 00:04:42,968
- Safe travels

82
00:04:43,239 --> 00:04:45,919
(Crowd murmur)

83
00:04:50,511 --> 00:04:52,488
Now go chase your love, worry-free!

84
00:04:52,513 --> 00:04:53,026
Shazdeh!

85
00:04:53,183 --> 00:04:54,082
Yes, dear?

86
00:04:54,107 --> 00:04:57,234
Tonight I’m making Aash Reshteh for Sir’s safe return.

87
00:04:57,259 --> 00:04:58,068
Don’t forget to come!

88
00:04:58,093 --> 00:04:58,776
Sardar!

89
00:04:58,801 --> 00:05:00,616
Tonight Sir’s house, Aash Reshteh cooked!

90
00:05:00,692 --> 00:05:02,465
You and Lady also kindly come.

91
00:05:02,490 --> 00:05:03,307
No! No! No!

92
00:05:03,332 --> 00:05:04,918
We not wishing to trouble you.

93
00:05:04,943 --> 00:05:06,094
Plenty other chances.

94
00:05:06,145 --> 00:05:07,868
Some other day, Inshallah!

95
00:05:08,237 --> 00:05:09,052
Moment!

96
00:05:09,077 --> 00:05:10,406
Sardar, no trouble!

97
00:05:10,431 --> 00:05:12,450
By your life, the lady will be upset kartahe!

98
00:05:12,582 --> 00:05:13,623
You won’t mind, ma’am?

99
00:05:14,399 --> 00:05:15,046
Well...

100
00:05:15,071 --> 00:05:17,279
They’re most welcome!

101
00:05:17,304 --> 00:05:18,487
What are you saying, woman!

102
00:05:18,939 --> 00:05:20,824
This Indian coming to Khan Dadash’s house tonight?

103
00:05:20,958 --> 00:05:21,738
Strange!

104
00:05:21,836 --> 00:05:23,319
This Asdollah has completely lost his mind!

105
00:05:23,658 --> 00:05:24,932
Bravo Sardar!

106
00:05:24,957 --> 00:05:26,330
You recited a very excellent poem! -Thank you!

107
00:05:27,031 --> 00:05:27,847
Hello!

108
00:05:28,005 --> 00:05:28,721
Mr Asadollah!

109
00:05:28,746 --> 00:05:31,840
Oh! My lady! Lady mahaarat khan!

110
00:05:32,396 --> 00:05:34,176
My dear! How are you?

111
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,999
Fine! Thank you! And, how are you?

112
00:05:37,715 --> 00:05:38,341
Fine!

113
00:05:38,734 --> 00:05:40,260
Tonight! You are our guest!

114
00:05:40,629 --> 00:05:42,202
Ash reshteh with laugh!

115
00:05:42,712 --> 00:05:43,272
Ok!

116
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:44,681
Oh, definitely!

117
00:05:44,802 --> 00:05:46,801
If Sardaar has no other engagements.

118
00:05:47,273 --> 00:05:47,849
Sardar!

119
00:05:48,013 --> 00:05:49,262
Lady agrees!

120
00:05:49,711 --> 00:05:52,154
You kindness kartahe,

121
00:05:52,179 --> 00:05:53,794
honoring our humble home.

122
00:05:53,819 --> 00:05:56,196
Tonight, much laughing kartahe!

123
00:05:56,221 --> 00:05:57,462
If the lady agrees,

124
00:05:57,487 --> 00:05:58,402
we also agree!

125
00:05:58,616 --> 00:05:59,378
Goodbye! -Yes!

126
00:05:59,403 --> 00:05:59,776
Byebye!

127
00:05:59,801 --> 00:06:00,441
Don’t come late!

128
00:06:06,819 --> 00:06:08,638
You were ogling her!

129
00:06:10,252 --> 00:06:11,757
Damn you!

130
00:06:11,961 --> 00:06:12,714
Hello!

131
00:06:13,459 --> 00:06:14,203
Byebye!

132
00:06:15,937 --> 00:06:16,656
Oh honey!

133
00:06:17,547 --> 00:06:19,148
Tonight, eyes to yourself!

134
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:20,253
For what?

135
00:06:21,156 --> 00:06:23,546
This Sardar has two cobras in his house,

136
00:06:23,571 --> 00:06:24,683
kept in a cage!

137
00:06:25,074 --> 00:06:26,853
Whoever looks lewdly at his wife,

138
00:06:26,878 --> 00:06:27,706
at night he takes a snake

139
00:06:27,731 --> 00:06:29,405
and throws it into his bed!

140
00:06:30,411 --> 00:06:31,656
Really?! - Yes!

141
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:33,371
By God!

142
00:06:34,057 --> 00:06:35,464
Don’t think I’m joking!

143
00:06:35,489 --> 00:06:36,825
Want me to take you right now and show you?

144
00:06:36,898 --> 00:06:38,194
Are you serious, Asdollah?

145
00:06:38,529 --> 00:06:39,744
On your life!

146
00:06:39,896 --> 00:06:41,564
Nobody knows that in their house

147
00:06:41,589 --> 00:06:42,781
they keep snakes!

148
00:06:43,149 --> 00:06:45,262
Lady Maharat-Khan herself told me!

149
00:06:45,674 --> 00:06:47,143
Tonight, Lady Maharat-Khan’s name,

150
00:06:47,168 --> 00:06:48,618
please don’t mention it in front of Aziz!

151
00:06:48,836 --> 00:06:50,924
Honestly, tomorrow I’ll have hell to pay with Aziz!

152
00:06:50,949 --> 00:06:51,883
She thinks

153
00:06:52,035 --> 00:06:53,707
I’ve fallen in love with the English woman!

154
00:06:54,001 --> 00:06:55,801
Last time too, it was because of your jokes

155
00:06:55,826 --> 00:06:58,096
that she came to bed with a kitchen knife!

156
00:06:58,121 --> 00:06:59,691
Moment!

157
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,317
Good grief!

158
00:07:05,016 --> 00:07:07,080
- Don’t tease him so much, Asdollah

159
00:07:07,919 --> 00:07:08,511
What’s with you?

160
00:07:08,535 --> 00:07:09,862
What’s so funny? Huh?

161
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:10,556
You don’t know how Uncle Asdollah

162
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:12,954
teases Dustali-Khan!

163
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:16,988
Who is that?

164
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,930
Looks like Aqa Seyed Abolghasem’s son!

165
00:07:19,955 --> 00:07:21,156
What does he want at this time of night?

166
00:07:21,181 --> 00:07:21,456
Hum?

167
00:07:21,481 --> 00:07:22,064
I don’t know!

168
00:07:25,750 --> 00:07:26,676
Salaam-Alaikum

169
00:07:26,701 --> 00:07:27,260
Salaam!

170
00:07:29,599 --> 00:07:30,881
Is your Agha Jan here?

171
00:07:30,931 --> 00:07:32,106
Yes, do you need him?

172
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:33,314
Can you call him?

173
00:07:33,819 --> 00:07:34,501
Sure.

174
00:07:34,525 --> 00:07:36,582
- Poor Dustali!

175
00:07:39,073 --> 00:07:41,372
(Murmur of the guests)

176
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:45,558
Agha Joon!

177
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:48,632
What is it, son?

178
00:07:48,889 --> 00:07:49,817
Someone’s at the door for you!

179
00:07:49,842 --> 00:07:50,349
Who is it?

180
00:07:50,681 --> 00:07:51,167
The son...

181
00:07:51,191 --> 00:07:51,885
Quietly!

182
00:07:52,719 --> 00:07:54,507
It’s the son of Aqa Seyed Abolghasem!

183
00:08:00,339 --> 00:08:01,913
What does that rascal want with me?

184
00:08:01,938 --> 00:08:02,599
How should I know!

185
00:08:04,919 --> 00:08:05,915
- How dare you!

186
00:08:08,516 --> 00:08:09,252
Salaam, Mr. Doctor!

187
00:08:09,276 --> 00:08:10,103
What is it? What do you want?

188
00:08:10,634 --> 00:08:11,100
What is it?

189
00:08:11,125 --> 00:08:13,406
Sir, my father asks you to come right away...

190
00:08:13,431 --> 00:08:13,874
No way!

191
00:08:13,905 --> 00:08:15,130
Your father can forget it!

192
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:17,578
Tell him I won’t set foot in that lowlife Seyed’s house!

193
00:08:17,926 --> 00:08:18,968
The matter is important!

194
00:08:18,992 --> 00:08:20,786
I beg you, please come!

195
00:08:21,588 --> 00:08:21,901
What is it?

196
00:08:22,332 --> 00:08:25,618
It’s news about Sir’s pilgrimage to Qom!

197
00:08:28,759 --> 00:08:30,292
Wait at the door! I’m coming! - Yes, sir!

198
00:08:30,909 --> 00:08:31,670
Agha Joon!

199
00:08:32,253 --> 00:08:33,580
Can Leili and I come with you?

200
00:08:33,605 --> 00:08:35,853
You’d leave the party to go to the preacher’s house?

201
00:08:35,910 --> 00:08:36,443
We got tired.

202
00:08:36,481 --> 00:08:38,328
We want to walk in the alleys a bit.

203
00:08:39,345 --> 00:08:40,060
Very well! You come.

204
00:08:40,198 --> 00:08:41,298
But Leili stays!

205
00:08:41,606 --> 00:08:42,258
Leili Joon!

206
00:08:42,404 --> 00:08:43,806
If anyone asks for me,

207
00:08:43,913 --> 00:08:46,092
say I went home on business, back soon!

208
00:08:46,117 --> 00:08:48,211
Well, my dear! - Okay. If you say so, I’ll stay

209
00:08:49,498 --> 00:08:50,591
You won’t mind if I go?

210
00:08:50,616 --> 00:08:50,923
No!

211
00:08:50,948 --> 00:08:51,299
So I’ll go?

212
00:08:51,324 --> 00:08:51,636
Yes.

213
00:08:51,661 --> 00:08:52,091
Hey!

214
00:08:52,349 --> 00:08:53,071
Saeid!

215
00:08:53,315 --> 00:08:54,264
Coming, Agha Joon!

216
00:08:54,804 --> 00:08:55,799
Later I’ll tell you everything!

217
00:08:55,823 --> 00:08:56,737
Very well, go!

218
00:08:56,762 --> 00:08:57,913
But come back soon!

219
00:08:58,337 --> 00:08:59,272
Hurry up!

220
00:08:59,478 --> 00:08:59,978
Run!

221
00:09:00,165 --> 00:09:02,165
♪ Traditional music ♪

222
00:09:10,538 --> 00:09:11,184
Close the door.

223
00:09:12,671 --> 00:09:13,591
Lead the way!

224
00:09:51,999 --> 00:09:53,544
You have honored us, Mr. Doctor!

225
00:09:53,569 --> 00:09:54,095
Please come.

226
00:09:54,119 --> 00:09:55,202
It’s a humble home! - Where? Where is he?

227
00:09:55,334 --> 00:09:57,057
Please come. He’s sitting in the main hall.

228
00:09:57,082 --> 00:09:57,936
Son, hurry!

229
00:09:57,966 --> 00:09:58,558
We’re late!

230
00:09:58,582 --> 00:09:59,642
Make haste! Come on!

231
00:10:01,890 --> 00:10:02,406
Oh!

232
00:10:02,872 --> 00:10:04,385
Sir, what are you doing here? - Hello, uncle

233
00:10:04,410 --> 00:10:05,585
Didn’t you go on pilgrimage?

234
00:10:05,609 --> 00:10:07,060
Come in and I’ll explain!

235
00:10:07,085 --> 00:10:08,824
Salaam-Alaikum Mr. Doctor! - Salaam-Alaikum

236
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:10,714
I’d told the Seyed’s son

237
00:10:10,738 --> 00:10:11,623
you should come alone!

238
00:10:11,648 --> 00:10:13,352
Why did you bring Saeid with you?

239
00:10:14,786 --> 00:10:16,026
His son said nothing!

240
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:17,985
He only said Aqa Seyed Abolghasem wanted me!

241
00:10:18,932 --> 00:10:21,692
I need a private word with you!

242
00:10:21,716 --> 00:10:23,301
It’s no place for children!

243
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,253
Saeid Joon!

244
00:10:26,465 --> 00:10:28,196
Go wait for me in the yard

245
00:10:34,335 --> 00:10:36,627
Sir, I missed you so much!

246
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,850
And if Sir asked,

247
00:10:39,874 --> 00:10:41,061
say I’m at a sermon!

248
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:42,929
If they want tea or anything,

249
00:10:42,953 --> 00:10:44,754
tell Mash Ghasem to get it from my wife!

250
00:10:45,123 --> 00:10:47,025
Come bolt the door, son!

251
00:10:47,139 --> 00:10:47,581
Yes.

252
00:10:47,859 --> 00:10:48,932
Bless you!

253
00:10:54,728 --> 00:10:57,190
When I say the English

254
00:10:57,215 --> 00:11:00,473
never take their eyes off me for a minute,

255
00:11:00,577 --> 00:11:02,172
my relatives say,

256
00:11:02,197 --> 00:11:03,805
you’re exaggerating!

257
00:11:03,830 --> 00:11:05,516
you suspect everyone!

258
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,036
Didn’t you see

259
00:11:07,061 --> 00:11:08,276
how this spy of theirs

260
00:11:08,301 --> 00:11:11,375
found out my plan to go to Nishapur!

261
00:11:11,643 --> 00:11:12,985
If not for Sir,

262
00:11:13,009 --> 00:11:15,449
we’d have died of fright!

263
00:11:15,474 --> 00:11:17,646
Qasem, let me talk!

264
00:11:17,671 --> 00:11:17,915
Yes!

265
00:11:18,143 --> 00:11:18,759
You were saying.

266
00:11:18,783 --> 00:11:21,320
This morning, in Dabir-Khaghan’s car,

267
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:23,058
I supposedly left for Qom!

268
00:11:23,083 --> 00:11:25,079
Only you and I know

269
00:11:25,103 --> 00:11:27,410
that I’m headed for Nishapur!

270
00:11:27,881 --> 00:11:29,305
Then this Indian comes,

271
00:11:29,329 --> 00:11:30,600
stands in the middle of the alley,

272
00:11:30,625 --> 00:11:31,393
and recites a poem:

273
00:11:31,417 --> 00:11:34,622
“My beloved is in Lahore and I am in Nishapur”

274
00:11:34,653 --> 00:11:36,494
Is this coincidence?

275
00:11:36,805 --> 00:11:38,558
Do you really think the Indian Sardar,

276
00:11:38,582 --> 00:11:39,588
just by chance,

277
00:11:39,612 --> 00:11:40,962
came up with this poem?

278
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:42,579
Oh God!

279
00:11:42,603 --> 00:11:45,547
Grant us a chance to go to Imamzadeh Hassan once,

280
00:11:45,572 --> 00:11:46,863
to vow a candle,

281
00:11:46,888 --> 00:11:48,843
so he brings the English to ruin!

282
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:49,939
Strange!

283
00:11:50,388 --> 00:11:52,299
I’d give my life for Imamzadeh Hassan!

284
00:11:52,324 --> 00:11:53,763
He works such miracles!

285
00:11:54,118 --> 00:11:56,752
I remember we had a fellow from our town... - Qasem!

286
00:11:56,777 --> 00:11:57,098
- Yes

287
00:11:57,219 --> 00:12:00,315
Qasem, will you let me talk?

288
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:01,253
Yes! Please, go on!

289
00:12:01,792 --> 00:12:04,507
Today when we left the city,

290
00:12:06,646 --> 00:12:10,207
we couldn’t find the Nishapur road, however hard we looked!

291
00:12:10,567 --> 00:12:13,791
So I took the back roads here!

292
00:12:14,639 --> 00:12:18,032
Because I thought if I went home,

293
00:12:19,253 --> 00:12:22,823
this Indian would report to London!

294
00:12:23,566 --> 00:12:25,293
I assure you

295
00:12:25,318 --> 00:12:27,366
that with binoculars,

296
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:30,257
he’s sitting at his window right now,

297
00:12:30,571 --> 00:12:32,326
watching my house...

298
00:12:32,351 --> 00:12:34,631
so that if anything happens, - Oh, Sir

299
00:12:34,656 --> 00:12:36,222
- Oh Sir

300
00:12:37,661 --> 00:12:40,054
This Indian Sardar Maharat-Khan,

301
00:12:40,078 --> 00:12:42,275
right now is in your house!

302
00:12:42,506 --> 00:12:44,207
He is sitting in your house,

303
00:12:44,232 --> 00:12:46,141
eating the Aash Reshteh made for your safe journey!

304
00:12:46,166 --> 00:12:46,754
Sardar?

305
00:12:47,232 --> 00:12:48,036
Sardar? - Yes!

306
00:12:48,246 --> 00:12:49,840
Sardar Maharat-Khan?

307
00:12:49,865 --> 00:12:50,479
Yes!

308
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:52,643
He is sitting in my house?

309
00:12:52,910 --> 00:12:54,112
Qasem, did you hear?

310
00:12:54,137 --> 00:12:54,662
Yes Sir!

311
00:12:54,686 --> 00:12:57,537
They’ve stabbed me in the back!

312
00:12:57,833 --> 00:12:59,169
How beautifully put!

313
00:12:59,895 --> 00:13:01,695
A stab in the back!

314
00:13:02,739 --> 00:13:05,508
Sir, this Indian Sardar is a nobody!

315
00:13:05,992 --> 00:13:08,249
To complete your file, the English

316
00:13:08,273 --> 00:13:09,818
have a thousand ways!

317
00:13:10,252 --> 00:13:13,470
From day one, I never really suspected

318
00:13:13,821 --> 00:13:15,207
the Indian Sardar Maharat-Khan.

319
00:13:16,650 --> 00:13:18,901
But tonight in your house,

320
00:13:19,975 --> 00:13:21,489
about his wife,

321
00:13:21,513 --> 00:13:22,393
I got suspicious!

322
00:13:23,581 --> 00:13:24,694
His wife? - Uh-huh

323
00:13:25,752 --> 00:13:27,001
Tonight? - Yes

324
00:13:27,823 --> 00:13:28,769
In my house?

325
00:13:28,794 --> 00:13:30,869
Tonight, right in your house,

326
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:32,042
she was staring hard

327
00:13:32,066 --> 00:13:33,200
at a photo of you!

328
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,601
Sardar’s wife? - Yes

329
00:13:35,821 --> 00:13:37,363
This English woman? - Uh-huh

330
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,162
In my house! - Uh-huh

331
00:13:39,348 --> 00:13:44,289
So my house has become English war headquarters!

332
00:13:44,438 --> 00:13:47,399
Who let these people into my house?

333
00:13:47,424 --> 00:13:48,782
Oh, oh, oh, oh....

334
00:13:48,806 --> 00:13:49,874
Sir, Sir! What happened?

335
00:13:49,911 --> 00:13:50,714
What happened? - Mash Ghasem!

336
00:13:50,845 --> 00:13:52,607
Run and fetch Doctor Naser Al-Hokama!

337
00:13:52,632 --> 00:13:52,934
Yes!

338
00:13:52,959 --> 00:13:54,350
No! No!

339
00:13:54,513 --> 00:13:58,427
Doctor Naser Al-Hokama is a lackey of the English!

340
00:13:58,894 --> 00:14:03,125
His cousin works in the English oil company!

341
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:06,679
Give me the bowl of water!

342
00:14:07,339 --> 00:14:08,331
Oh...

343
00:14:08,951 --> 00:14:09,877
Give it to me...

344
00:14:11,073 --> 00:14:12,212
Take a sip!

345
00:14:12,703 --> 00:14:14,899
What infidels these English are,

346
00:14:15,024 --> 00:14:16,797
May their shifty eyes go blind!

347
00:14:16,956 --> 00:14:18,323
♪ Sad traditional music ♪

348
00:14:18,643 --> 00:14:20,207
May God humiliate them!

349
00:14:20,618 --> 00:14:26,025
In the claws of a bloodthirsty lion,

350
00:14:27,242 --> 00:14:31,201
what choice is there but to surrender and accept!

351
00:14:31,756 --> 00:14:33,993
Surrender? That’s not like you!

352
00:14:34,073 --> 00:14:36,350
You’ve fought all your life!

353
00:14:36,706 --> 00:14:38,665
Don’t you remember what Napoleon said?

354
00:14:40,031 --> 00:14:43,897
Great men are known in hard times!

355
00:14:44,199 --> 00:14:45,603
You’re right!

356
00:14:48,646 --> 00:14:50,933
There’s no room for retreat!

357
00:14:53,212 --> 00:14:54,053
Meaning...

358
00:14:54,813 --> 00:14:57,697
There’s no way to retreat either!

359
00:14:59,776 --> 00:15:01,917
To continue the struggle,

360
00:15:03,423 --> 00:15:05,590
I must stay alive.

361
00:15:07,346 --> 00:15:08,694
The English,

362
00:15:09,339 --> 00:15:11,736
with the terror they have of me,

363
00:15:12,996 --> 00:15:15,660
will never leave me alone!

364
00:15:15,716 --> 00:15:18,855
♪ Military trumpet ♪

365
00:15:27,982 --> 00:15:28,884
God help us!

366
00:15:28,908 --> 00:15:31,582
They’ve already cut millions of people in two!

367
00:15:31,753 --> 00:15:33,208
Sir, just today,

368
00:15:33,232 --> 00:15:34,622
outside the gate,

369
00:15:35,249 --> 00:15:36,771
at a coffeehouse,

370
00:15:36,796 --> 00:15:39,306
we stopped for tea!

371
00:15:40,681 --> 00:15:42,293
Travelers from the south

372
00:15:42,408 --> 00:15:46,540
were telling such tales of their atrocities!

373
00:15:46,794 --> 00:15:48,440
God have mercy on Ghias Abad!

374
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,383
The rest of Iran is one thing,

375
00:15:50,468 --> 00:15:52,121
Ghias Abad is another!

376
00:15:52,559 --> 00:15:55,562
The Ghias Abadis really went after the English...

377
00:15:55,587 --> 00:15:56,523
Shut up Qasem!

378
00:15:56,547 --> 00:15:59,399
Let’s worry about our own misery!

379
00:16:00,388 --> 00:16:02,680
What do you think we should do now?

380
00:16:03,632 --> 00:16:05,168
The best way is

381
00:16:05,192 --> 00:16:06,098
to use one enemy

382
00:16:06,122 --> 00:16:07,771
against the other!

383
00:16:08,651 --> 00:16:10,491
In my view, your salvation lies

384
00:16:10,516 --> 00:16:11,565
with the Germans!

385
00:16:11,966 --> 00:16:12,935
The Germans?

386
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:13,402
Uh-huh!

387
00:16:13,426 --> 00:16:15,518
They no longer have influence in Iran!

388
00:16:16,010 --> 00:16:17,591
Oh, but they do!

389
00:16:18,333 --> 00:16:20,744
They’ve only seemingly left!

390
00:16:22,318 --> 00:16:25,064
But a huge secret organization

391
00:16:25,088 --> 00:16:27,473
they have right here in Tehran!

392
00:16:30,874 --> 00:16:33,000
You write a letter to them.

393
00:16:33,118 --> 00:16:34,655
Write a letter to whom?

394
00:16:34,823 --> 00:16:35,772
To Hitler!

395
00:16:35,894 --> 00:16:36,687
Long live!

396
00:16:36,918 --> 00:16:38,651
If there’s one real man in the world,

397
00:16:38,690 --> 00:16:40,111
it’s our own Hitler-Khan!

398
00:16:41,573 --> 00:16:44,374
You must write a letter to Hitler,

399
00:16:44,438 --> 00:16:46,624
asking for protection these few months,

400
00:16:46,649 --> 00:16:47,760
until their army arrives.

401
00:16:48,245 --> 00:16:50,265
I have no doubt the German army

402
00:16:50,396 --> 00:16:53,156
will be at the gates of Tehran in three or four months!

403
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:55,459
Qasem, get up and bring a pen and inkwell!

404
00:16:55,490 --> 00:16:55,898
Yes!

405
00:16:56,246 --> 00:16:58,413
The Germans would never abandon us!

406
00:16:58,923 --> 00:17:00,378
They’re our allies!

407
00:17:01,326 --> 00:17:02,359
Just write the letter,

408
00:17:02,749 --> 00:17:04,846
and you’re done!

409
00:17:06,626 --> 00:17:08,331
And bring something to write on.

410
00:17:08,355 --> 00:17:09,156
Bring that book stand. - Yes, sir!

411
00:17:10,526 --> 00:17:13,125
If the Germans have stepped aside for now,

412
00:17:13,219 --> 00:17:14,294
it’s because they mean

413
00:17:14,318 --> 00:17:16,191
to pull a fast one on the Allies!

414
00:17:16,912 --> 00:17:18,766
You’ll see, before long,

415
00:17:19,009 --> 00:17:21,353
how the Russian and English armies

416
00:17:21,452 --> 00:17:22,500
get caught off guard!

417
00:17:22,525 --> 00:17:23,989
It’s a bit dark in here, too!

418
00:17:24,606 --> 00:17:26,392
Qasem, bring that lamp closer.

419
00:17:26,417 --> 00:17:27,310
Yes. - Put it right down here.

420
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:32,348
Closer!

421
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:47,317
Please write!

422
00:17:48,053 --> 00:17:48,628
Hold on!

423
00:17:48,813 --> 00:17:49,893
My hand trembles a little!

424
00:17:50,039 --> 00:17:52,440
Try to write very neatly and legibly,

425
00:17:52,523 --> 00:17:53,989
so that nothing

426
00:17:54,134 --> 00:17:56,440
is unclear to the Leader.

427
00:17:56,733 --> 00:17:57,830
How should I address it?

428
00:17:57,855 --> 00:18:00,207
Very respectfully, at the top of the page, please write:

429
00:18:00,478 --> 00:18:03,047
To the blessed presence of His Excellency,

430
00:18:03,229 --> 00:18:05,043
Adolf Hitler!

431
00:18:07,159 --> 00:18:08,950
May his glory last!

432
00:18:12,187 --> 00:18:14,771
Great Leader of Germany!

433
00:18:20,424 --> 00:18:21,086
After...

434
00:18:21,233 --> 00:18:21,893
offering...

435
00:18:21,999 --> 00:18:22,939
my devotion...

436
00:18:24,310 --> 00:18:27,654
I humbly submit to Your Excellency,

437
00:18:28,994 --> 00:18:30,934
submit...

438
00:18:31,086 --> 00:18:31,827
that your devoted servant

439
00:18:31,987 --> 00:18:33,321
is certain

440
00:18:37,592 --> 00:18:40,792
that Your Excellency... of the struggles...

441
00:18:44,277 --> 00:18:49,114
long and stubborn, of your servant and his late father,

442
00:18:49,271 --> 00:18:50,426
- God rest his soul

443
00:18:51,591 --> 00:18:53,249
- God rest his soul. - Yes!

444
00:18:53,274 --> 00:18:54,721
May he rest in peace!

445
00:18:55,566 --> 00:18:56,551
Please write...

446
00:18:56,857 --> 00:18:59,011
against English colonialism,

447
00:19:00,004 --> 00:19:02,434
is well informed!

448
00:19:03,732 --> 00:19:04,502
- Uh-huh!

449
00:19:04,593 --> 00:19:05,513
Nevertheless,

450
00:19:05,537 --> 00:19:06,836
if I may be so bold,

451
00:19:07,775 --> 00:19:11,005
an account of his struggles

452
00:19:12,424 --> 00:19:13,342
- his...

453
00:19:14,397 --> 00:19:16,583
is presented hereunder!

454
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,888
Presented hereunder! Aha!

455
00:19:20,913 --> 00:19:21,401
Aha!

456
00:19:21,808 --> 00:19:22,541
After that?

457
00:19:23,011 --> 00:19:25,549
Now describe the Kazeroon war,

458
00:19:25,819 --> 00:19:27,134
the Mamasani war,

459
00:19:27,844 --> 00:19:30,059
your struggles with the English...

460
00:19:30,268 --> 00:19:31,368
Please write!

461
00:19:33,039 --> 00:19:33,495
Sir!

462
00:19:33,754 --> 00:19:36,568
Then also mention Sardar Maharat-Khan and...

463
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:38,161
his English wife!

464
00:19:38,830 --> 00:19:40,320
Of course, we’re not certain

465
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:42,347
that this Indian is an English spy!

466
00:19:42,372 --> 00:19:44,619
What do you mean, not certain?

467
00:19:44,937 --> 00:19:46,479
He’s their agent!

468
00:19:46,637 --> 00:19:49,920
Specifically assigned to watch me!

469
00:19:49,945 --> 00:19:50,257
Well!

470
00:19:50,596 --> 00:19:51,773
Then write

471
00:19:51,798 --> 00:19:52,504
that you’re sure

472
00:19:52,529 --> 00:19:53,752
he is their agent

473
00:19:54,476 --> 00:19:55,250
In any case,

474
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,756
describe your situation well

475
00:19:56,858 --> 00:19:58,933
for the Leader of Germany.

476
00:19:58,958 --> 00:19:59,400
Of course!

477
00:19:59,424 --> 00:20:01,372
And don’t forget the end of the letter!

478
00:20:01,514 --> 00:20:02,516
Definitely write:

479
00:20:02,719 --> 00:20:03,554
Heil Hitler!

480
00:20:04,013 --> 00:20:05,602
What does that mean?

481
00:20:06,092 --> 00:20:08,078
It means long live Hitler!

482
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:09,496
Long live!

483
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:12,023
Well!

484
00:20:12,281 --> 00:20:12,923
Let me see!

485
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:14,915
If Hitler wants

486
00:20:14,939 --> 00:20:17,148
to save me from the English,

487
00:20:17,312 --> 00:20:19,241
what do you think he’ll do?

488
00:20:19,392 --> 00:20:21,467
For him it’s a piece of cake!

489
00:20:21,792 --> 00:20:23,788
Not tomorrow night, the night after!

490
00:20:23,936 --> 00:20:25,954
A German Junkers plane

491
00:20:30,350 --> 00:20:32,418
in the desert outside the Qazvin gate

492
00:20:32,442 --> 00:20:33,336
will land!

493
00:20:33,361 --> 00:20:34,902
and whisks you away!

494
00:20:35,439 --> 00:20:38,137
Hitler’s agents have done this a thousand times!

495
00:20:38,866 --> 00:20:41,131
Well, then where will they take me?

496
00:20:41,204 --> 00:20:42,340
Berlin!

497
00:20:42,586 --> 00:20:43,792
After two or three months,

498
00:20:43,816 --> 00:20:45,935
with the victorious German army,

499
00:20:45,972 --> 00:20:47,080
you’ll return to Tehran! - Sir...

500
00:20:47,887 --> 00:20:49,574
Sir, what about me?

501
00:20:55,526 --> 00:20:57,058
Could I ask

502
00:20:57,083 --> 00:20:57,712
that

503
00:20:57,773 --> 00:20:59,601
Qasem come with me too?

504
00:20:59,885 --> 00:21:01,927
So we go to Berlin together? - No problem!

505
00:21:02,273 --> 00:21:05,177
Then write two lines about Mash Ghasem

506
00:21:05,235 --> 00:21:07,328
and how his life is in danger.

507
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,302
Why the long face, Mash Ghasem?

508
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:12,657
How could you not go with Sir?

509
00:21:13,114 --> 00:21:15,812
From here to Berlin is sooo far,

510
00:21:15,946 --> 00:21:17,007
Honestly, Sir, why lie!

511
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:18,896
The grave is this close!

512
00:21:19,822 --> 00:21:21,959
The English have a grudge against us too!

513
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:24,580
Remember, in the Kazeroon war,

514
00:21:24,605 --> 00:21:26,331
we killed a few English!

515
00:21:27,214 --> 00:21:28,882
With one blow of the sword,

516
00:21:28,907 --> 00:21:30,261
we cut off a colonel’s head

517
00:21:30,286 --> 00:21:32,228
and threw it at his regiment’s feet!

518
00:21:33,311 --> 00:21:35,217
We struck so fast he didn’t even notice!

519
00:21:36,092 --> 00:21:38,097
When we threw the shameless bastard’s head down,

520
00:21:38,122 --> 00:21:39,929
he cursed our mothers and sisters for half an hour!

521
00:21:40,586 --> 00:21:41,679
So we had no choice

522
00:21:41,703 --> 00:21:43,904
but to stuff a handkerchief down his throat...!

523
00:21:43,929 --> 00:21:45,515
Oh! Shut up already!

524
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:47,201
Hold on, Qasem!

525
00:21:47,605 --> 00:21:48,660
With stunts like these,

526
00:21:48,684 --> 00:21:50,750
you’ll disgrace me in Berlin!

527
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:53,960
Well, how will you get this letter to Hitler

528
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:54,758
without delay?

529
00:21:54,783 --> 00:21:57,053
I know one of their spies

530
00:21:57,243 --> 00:21:58,757
who’ll send your exact letter

531
00:21:58,782 --> 00:22:00,608
to them by wireless.

532
00:22:01,107 --> 00:22:02,149
Rest assured,

533
00:22:02,173 --> 00:22:03,967
within a few days, they’ll contact you.

534
00:22:04,485 --> 00:22:07,406
Well, what do I do until they contact me?

535
00:22:10,196 --> 00:22:11,988
You better return home.

536
00:22:12,395 --> 00:22:14,091
Act as if nothing has happened!

537
00:22:14,741 --> 00:22:17,442
Be friendly with Sardar Maharat-Khan, too.

538
00:22:17,823 --> 00:22:20,475
Say the car broke down on the Qom road

539
00:22:20,586 --> 00:22:22,103
and you had to come back to Tehran!

540
00:22:23,390 --> 00:22:24,064
In fact,

541
00:22:24,169 --> 00:22:25,987
if this Sardar Maharat-Khan,

542
00:22:26,012 --> 00:22:27,928
really is an English agent,

543
00:22:28,626 --> 00:22:30,258
it’s better he reports

544
00:22:30,283 --> 00:22:31,794
that you’re at home,

545
00:22:31,990 --> 00:22:34,622
so the English stop worrying about you!

546
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,177
I’d better get back!

547
00:22:37,525 --> 00:22:39,116
Make a clean copy of this letter!

548
00:22:39,566 --> 00:22:40,620
Half an hour later,

549
00:22:40,645 --> 00:22:42,042
tired and dusty,

550
00:22:42,113 --> 00:22:42,787
go back home!

551
00:22:43,059 --> 00:22:44,172
And don’t worry about a thing!

552
00:22:44,610 --> 00:22:46,163
Rushed jobs

553
00:22:46,187 --> 00:22:48,691
always go wrong somewhere.

554
00:22:48,956 --> 00:22:51,635
If their representative wants to contact me,

555
00:22:51,710 --> 00:22:54,536
how will I know it’s really him?

556
00:22:55,023 --> 00:22:56,171
You’re right.

557
00:22:56,515 --> 00:22:57,697
In such a situation,

558
00:22:57,721 --> 00:22:59,630
one must think of everything.

559
00:22:59,816 --> 00:23:00,967
Better pick a name,

560
00:23:00,992 --> 00:23:03,289
a sign, a code, something!

561
00:23:04,204 --> 00:23:06,590
How about we choose a number?

562
00:23:06,615 --> 00:23:07,387
For example,

563
00:23:07,759 --> 00:23:10,274
one thousand and three hundred and ninety and ....

564
00:23:10,299 --> 00:23:10,937
No no no Sir!

565
00:23:10,961 --> 00:23:12,460
The coffeehouse at the turn of Ghias Abad!

566
00:23:12,566 --> 00:23:13,919
No, my dear!

567
00:23:14,953 --> 00:23:15,349
But,

568
00:23:15,373 --> 00:23:16,909
the number must be written somewhere

569
00:23:16,934 --> 00:23:18,138
so you don’t forget!

570
00:23:18,639 --> 00:23:19,812
In such a situation,

571
00:23:19,836 --> 00:23:21,477
writing things down isn’t wise either!

572
00:23:21,502 --> 00:23:22,130
- Yes!

573
00:23:22,155 --> 00:23:24,255
It could fall into the hands of their spies!

574
00:23:24,342 --> 00:23:25,002
Yes!

575
00:23:27,428 --> 00:23:29,475
How about the name of one of the relatives?

576
00:23:30,039 --> 00:23:31,491
Mr. Dustali-Khan!

577
00:23:31,947 --> 00:23:32,714
Not bad!

578
00:23:34,144 --> 00:23:34,652
But,

579
00:23:34,910 --> 00:23:37,503
a bare name isn’t enough!

580
00:23:38,756 --> 00:23:40,382
They may guess!

581
00:23:40,759 --> 00:23:43,252
We need to think of a sentence, something

582
00:23:43,331 --> 00:23:45,120
the enemy’s spies can’t guess!

583
00:23:46,439 --> 00:23:47,218
Yes!

584
00:23:47,542 --> 00:23:48,136
Yes!

585
00:23:50,453 --> 00:23:52,173
Let me think a little.

586
00:24:00,283 --> 00:24:01,352
How about...

587
00:24:01,965 --> 00:24:03,207
no, no, no!

588
00:24:03,232 --> 00:24:05,633
The late Great Sir,

589
00:24:05,657 --> 00:24:06,187
with...

590
00:24:06,211 --> 00:24:07,124
who’d be good?

591
00:24:07,149 --> 00:24:07,515
Aha!

592
00:24:07,638 --> 00:24:11,270
with Marlene Dietrich, eats bozbash stew!

593
00:24:11,349 --> 00:24:12,814
Great Sir? - Yes!

594
00:24:13,128 --> 00:24:14,128
Don’t blaspheme!

595
00:24:14,153 --> 00:24:15,036
I’m ready

596
00:24:15,147 --> 00:24:18,944
to hang from an English gallows,

597
00:24:18,969 --> 00:24:21,170
but I’ll never agree

598
00:24:21,254 --> 00:24:23,658
that the late Great Sir’s name

599
00:24:23,683 --> 00:24:25,703
and the name of some loose woman

600
00:24:25,727 --> 00:24:26,981
be put side by side!

601
00:24:27,359 --> 00:24:28,518
God forgive me!

602
00:24:28,542 --> 00:24:29,138
Sir!

603
00:24:29,162 --> 00:24:31,491
Now why are you shouting at me like this?

604
00:24:31,990 --> 00:24:33,343
Forget about it, then.

605
00:24:33,511 --> 00:24:35,025
It’s not even certain the English want

606
00:24:35,049 --> 00:24:36,358
to take revenge on you.

607
00:24:36,839 --> 00:24:38,010
Perhaps after all this time,

608
00:24:38,035 --> 00:24:39,638
they’ve forgiven your sins!

609
00:24:39,663 --> 00:24:41,040
Forgiven my sins?

610
00:24:41,065 --> 00:24:43,302
Why would you say that?

611
00:24:43,607 --> 00:24:46,232
You know better than anyone

612
00:24:46,257 --> 00:24:51,001
what terrible plans the English have for me!

613
00:24:51,026 --> 00:24:53,385
Then why are you being so stubborn?

614
00:24:54,040 --> 00:24:56,226
Do you think if Napoleon

615
00:24:56,276 --> 00:24:58,954
could have escaped exile on such a condition,

616
00:24:59,041 --> 00:24:59,714
he would have hesitated?

617
00:25:00,745 --> 00:25:02,839
You don’t belong only to yourself!

618
00:25:03,482 --> 00:25:05,115
A great family,

619
00:25:05,499 --> 00:25:06,416
a city,

620
00:25:06,739 --> 00:25:07,878
a country,

621
00:25:07,902 --> 00:25:09,558
are waiting for your sacrifice!

622
00:25:09,938 --> 00:25:10,725
You’re too kind!

623
00:25:11,035 --> 00:25:11,435
Good night!

624
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:11,710
Sir,

625
00:25:11,915 --> 00:25:13,908
it seems Mr. Doctor is right!

626
00:25:14,149 --> 00:25:16,534
Don’t do anything to offend Mr. Doctor!

627
00:25:16,981 --> 00:25:18,150
For the sake of the people,

628
00:25:18,354 --> 00:25:19,334
I accept!

629
00:25:20,052 --> 00:25:21,720
What must I write?

630
00:25:24,086 --> 00:25:26,003
At the end of the letter, please write:

631
00:25:26,286 --> 00:25:27,282
It is requested,

632
00:25:27,307 --> 00:25:29,182
that you kindly order

633
00:25:29,427 --> 00:25:31,491
that, to contact this servant

634
00:25:31,712 --> 00:25:33,883
and identifying your agent,

635
00:25:34,094 --> 00:25:36,175
the code sentence below,

636
00:25:36,371 --> 00:25:38,728
hereby brought to Your Excellency’s attention,

637
00:25:38,752 --> 00:25:39,701
be used.

638
00:25:40,287 --> 00:25:42,160
Then, in quotation marks, write:

639
00:25:42,992 --> 00:25:45,379
The late Great Sir,

640
00:25:45,708 --> 00:25:47,148
with Marlene Dietrich,

641
00:25:47,464 --> 00:25:49,398
eats bozbash stew.

642
00:25:49,692 --> 00:25:50,938
Much obliged!

643
00:25:51,753 --> 00:25:52,550
Good night!

644
00:25:52,832 --> 00:25:53,832
You’re very kind!

645
00:25:56,698 --> 00:25:57,458
Get up, let’s go!

646
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:09,486
Agha Joon! Agha Joon!

647
00:26:09,637 --> 00:26:10,172
Yes?

648
00:26:10,764 --> 00:26:12,261
Why didn’t Dear Uncle go to Qom?

649
00:26:12,540 --> 00:26:14,189
His car broke down on the way,

650
00:26:14,213 --> 00:26:15,085
so he came back.

651
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:17,543
Saeid, this week,

652
00:26:17,567 --> 00:26:18,662
did you get your pocket money?

653
00:26:18,687 --> 00:26:18,991
No!

654
00:26:19,180 --> 00:26:20,545
Remind me to pay you tomorrow.

655
00:26:20,570 --> 00:26:21,041
Also,

656
00:26:21,352 --> 00:26:23,407
don’t tell anyone about tonight!

657
00:26:23,432 --> 00:26:24,449
No, Agha Joon!

658
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:28,590
May God forgive you

659
00:26:28,906 --> 00:26:30,673
for saving your own life

660
00:26:30,698 --> 00:26:32,654
by making your late Great Sir

661
00:26:32,679 --> 00:26:34,114
turn in his grave.

662
00:26:53,329 --> 00:26:54,292
(Sound of the guests’ laughter)

663
00:26:54,316 --> 00:26:55,165
Well, well!

664
00:26:55,956 --> 00:26:57,295
Hello Saeid!

665
00:26:57,475 --> 00:26:57,929
Hello!

666
00:26:58,000 --> 00:26:59,203
You should’ve seen Uncle Asdollah

667
00:26:59,227 --> 00:27:00,766
and what he’s doing to Dustali-Khan!

668
00:27:01,046 --> 00:27:02,689
Well! The party’s still going!

669
00:27:02,714 --> 00:27:04,078
Sir! Where have you been! - We missed you!

670
00:27:04,103 --> 00:27:04,705
Hello. How are you?

671
00:27:04,729 --> 00:27:05,561
You missed it, I was

672
00:27:05,585 --> 00:27:06,519
telling a great story - Where were you?

673
00:27:06,550 --> 00:27:07,992
to our honored guests. - Out. I had business.

674
00:27:08,594 --> 00:27:11,294
So after all that trouble,

675
00:27:11,549 --> 00:27:15,132
Mr. Dustali-Khan was left alone with the girl!

676
00:27:15,157 --> 00:27:17,240
(Crowd laughter)

677
00:27:17,679 --> 00:27:19,477
May your eye not see a bad day,

678
00:27:19,520 --> 00:27:20,845
Honorable Sardar!

679
00:27:20,892 --> 00:27:24,858
Mr. Dustali-Khan’s nature is behot depressed!

680
00:27:24,883 --> 00:27:27,019
(Crowd laughter)

681
00:27:27,044 --> 00:27:28,596
Back when he was young,

682
00:27:28,620 --> 00:27:30,894
his nature is behot depressed!

683
00:27:31,231 --> 00:27:33,116
Now, woe is him!

684
00:27:33,742 --> 00:27:34,655
Dustali’s nature...

685
00:27:34,686 --> 00:27:37,442
is behot behot depressed!

686
00:27:37,467 --> 00:27:39,117
(Crowd laughter)

687
00:27:39,919 --> 00:27:41,761
Nothing doing at all!

688
00:27:42,170 --> 00:27:43,997
behot behot! What does he say?-

689
00:27:44,022 --> 00:27:46,317
Doostali, after all that trouble,

690
00:27:46,416 --> 00:27:48,416
was finally alone with the girl.

691
00:27:48,779 --> 00:27:50,252
Well, You should see!

692
00:27:50,712 --> 00:27:51,987
when he was young,

693
00:27:52,018 --> 00:27:54,065
he did not do anything about it.

694
00:27:54,455 --> 00:27:57,529
Now that is all ...

695
00:27:57,662 --> 00:27:59,652
(Crowd laughter)

696
00:28:00,906 --> 00:28:02,888
Asdollah, the Imamzadeh Qasem story,

697
00:28:02,912 --> 00:28:03,815
I’ll tell it too!

698
00:28:04,212 --> 00:28:04,872
Wonderful!

699
00:28:09,144 --> 00:28:11,090
Your attention, please!

700
00:28:11,115 --> 00:28:12,752
Ladies and gentlemen!

701
00:28:12,939 --> 00:28:14,449
Ladies and Gentlemen!

702
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:16,081
Our honored friend,

703
00:28:16,159 --> 00:28:17,292
the able speaker,

704
00:28:17,317 --> 00:28:18,468
the master of all of us,

705
00:28:18,492 --> 00:28:19,365
His Most Excellent Eminence,

706
00:28:19,389 --> 00:28:21,448
Honorable Mr. Dustali-Khan,

707
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:23,617
the story of Imamzadeh Qasem,

708
00:28:23,641 --> 00:28:25,804
to our dear and honored listeners, with commentary,

709
00:28:25,829 --> 00:28:26,649
will now recount!

710
00:28:26,673 --> 00:28:27,075
Dustali-Khan!

711
00:28:27,099 --> 00:28:27,900
The microphone is yours!

712
00:28:27,931 --> 00:28:29,239
Oh, drop it! (Guests’ laughter)

713
00:28:30,772 --> 00:28:32,505
Why? - If I tell, you’ll be shamed!

714
00:28:32,552 --> 00:28:33,900
Man, by not telling it,

715
00:28:33,925 --> 00:28:36,697
you’ve shamed me before the Sardar and the lady!

716
00:28:36,728 --> 00:28:39,371
Mr. Sardar and the lady are my guests tonight!

717
00:28:39,455 --> 00:28:39,802
Oh?

718
00:28:39,827 --> 00:28:42,662
Pity you didn’t charm them more! - What?

719
00:28:42,687 --> 00:28:44,305
Mr. Sardar and their lady,

720
00:28:44,330 --> 00:28:45,814
are the guests of all of us!

721
00:28:45,986 --> 00:28:48,239
In fact, they came at my invitation!

722
00:28:48,926 --> 00:28:50,148
What nerve you have!

723
00:28:50,664 --> 00:28:52,983
When you first asked, they refused!

724
00:28:53,061 --> 00:28:55,084
But when I insisted to them,

725
00:28:55,108 --> 00:28:55,873
they came!

726
00:28:56,970 --> 00:28:57,958
Now let’s suppose,

727
00:28:57,982 --> 00:28:59,519
Lady Maharat-Khan is my guest,

728
00:28:59,598 --> 00:29:00,889
and Mr. Sardar is your guest!

729
00:29:00,914 --> 00:29:02,736
(Crowd laughter)

730
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:03,878
Like hell!

731
00:29:04,434 --> 00:29:05,963
Mr. Sardar and their lady,

732
00:29:05,987 --> 00:29:07,602
came here by my invitation,

733
00:29:07,627 --> 00:29:08,689
and they are my guests!

734
00:29:08,818 --> 00:29:10,319
It’s got nothing to do with you!

735
00:29:10,535 --> 00:29:11,933
This husband and wife

736
00:29:12,075 --> 00:29:13,674
came for my sake!

737
00:29:13,954 --> 00:29:15,289
So where do you come in?

738
00:29:15,522 --> 00:29:17,737
Oh, oh, oh! Khan Dadash!

739
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:19,213
Daddy dear!

740
00:29:19,810 --> 00:29:21,493
My daughter! - Daddy dear!

741
00:29:21,517 --> 00:29:22,731
Leili, my dear!

742
00:29:22,831 --> 00:29:24,138
Hello, Khan Dadash!

743
00:29:24,163 --> 00:29:25,558
Hello sister!

744
00:29:25,583 --> 00:29:26,955
Blessed pilgrimage!

745
00:29:26,986 --> 00:29:27,816
Thank you very much!

746
00:29:27,959 --> 00:29:29,165
Hello Khan Dadash!

747
00:29:29,189 --> 00:29:31,213
Hello... brother! - How are you!

748
00:29:31,237 --> 00:29:32,452
How are you? - Thank you very much!

749
00:29:32,477 --> 00:29:33,434
Your plan worked!

750
00:29:33,470 --> 00:29:34,911
Didn’t I say he’d come back? - I can’t believe it!

751
00:29:35,039 --> 00:29:36,411
Thank you! Thank you!

752
00:29:36,591 --> 00:29:37,817
I’m happy to see you!

753
00:29:37,855 --> 00:29:39,382
Are you well, Khan Dadash? - Thank you very much!

754
00:29:44,442 --> 00:29:44,805
We are happy!

755
00:29:44,829 --> 00:29:45,769
How come you came back?

756
00:29:45,794 --> 00:29:47,346
Near the castle of Mamdali-Khan,

757
00:29:47,434 --> 00:29:48,611
the car broke down!

758
00:29:49,392 --> 00:29:51,160
It’s all for the best!

759
00:29:51,185 --> 00:29:53,052
There’s always another chance for pilgrimage!

760
00:29:53,077 --> 00:29:53,652
- Yes!

761
00:29:53,676 --> 00:29:54,486
All is well, Khan Dadash!

762
00:29:54,511 --> 00:29:56,260
God willing, we’ll go together next month!

763
00:29:56,285 --> 00:29:58,889
You, it seems, very quickly from Nishapur to Lahore

764
00:29:59,428 --> 00:30:00,592
have returned!

765
00:30:01,230 --> 00:30:02,238
Well, it’s a car!

766
00:30:02,262 --> 00:30:03,210
It breaks down.

767
00:30:04,926 --> 00:30:05,577
By the way,

768
00:30:05,675 --> 00:30:06,595
that letter

769
00:30:06,619 --> 00:30:10,013
you kindly wrote to the innkeeper

770
00:30:10,038 --> 00:30:10,863
was no use!

771
00:30:10,888 --> 00:30:12,471
Keep it, then!

772
00:30:12,496 --> 00:30:13,332
Welcome back!

773
00:30:16,039 --> 00:30:16,892
- He came back early!

774
00:30:16,917 --> 00:30:18,112
- How nice... I didn’t expect it at all...

775
00:30:19,572 --> 00:30:20,556
By the way...

776
00:30:20,586 --> 00:30:21,423
- No problem at all

777
00:30:21,448 --> 00:30:22,494
Where is Aziz Khanom?

778
00:30:22,686 --> 00:30:23,328
Shazdeh!

779
00:30:23,632 --> 00:30:26,197
Don’t tell me Dustali got rid of her tonight!

780
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:29,875
Lady Aziz-Saltaneh,

781
00:30:29,912 --> 00:30:32,418
went to Imamzadeh Davood to make a vow!

782
00:30:32,827 --> 00:30:34,414
To make a vow?

783
00:30:35,718 --> 00:30:37,951
Yes! To cure Dustali-Khan’s depression!

784
00:30:38,899 --> 00:30:39,768
As the Honorable Sardar put it,

785
00:30:39,792 --> 00:30:41,049
the nature of Mr. Dustali-Khan,

786
00:30:41,074 --> 00:30:42,834
unfortunately is behot depressed!

787
00:30:42,859 --> 00:30:45,422
(Crowd laughter)

788
00:30:45,447 --> 00:30:45,877
Wonderful!

789
00:30:45,902 --> 00:30:47,169
When I said, Asdollah?

790
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:49,764
I didn’t say you said it!

791
00:30:50,031 --> 00:30:51,664
I was quoting you!

792
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:55,503
Besides, you can tell from his face

793
00:30:55,661 --> 00:30:57,794
his nature, I swear, is behot depressed!

794
00:31:01,120 --> 00:31:02,734
Asdollah, I’ll punch you in the snout so hard

795
00:31:02,759 --> 00:31:04,194
your teeth will fall down your throat!

796
00:31:04,225 --> 00:31:04,786
Yes?

797
00:31:04,997 --> 00:31:05,687
What’s going on?

798
00:31:05,712 --> 00:31:06,820
Come on, we’re not fighting!

799
00:31:06,845 --> 00:31:07,822
Why are you taking offense?

800
00:31:07,846 --> 00:31:09,395
You’ve overdone it now!

801
00:31:09,719 --> 00:31:10,592
Enough from you too!

802
00:31:12,174 --> 00:31:13,565
Actually, your nature

803
00:31:13,589 --> 00:31:14,723
behot behot,

804
00:31:15,561 --> 00:31:16,667
is not depressed!

805
00:31:17,080 --> 00:31:17,842
Your nature,

806
00:31:17,872 --> 00:31:19,087
is behot active!

807
00:31:19,206 --> 00:31:20,415
In fact, your nature

808
00:31:20,704 --> 00:31:22,437
is like the mighty hero Rostam’s!

809
00:31:22,931 --> 00:31:26,007
(Crowd laughter and murmuring)

810
00:31:26,886 --> 00:31:28,106
Sir’s nature is like...

811
00:31:28,256 --> 00:31:28,986
I’ll prove it!

812
00:31:29,011 --> 00:31:30,086
Never mind! I’ll prove it!

813
00:31:30,117 --> 00:31:32,123
Leave the poor wretch alone!

814
00:31:32,737 --> 00:31:33,784
Either you must not speak,

815
00:31:33,816 --> 00:31:35,484
or if you do, you must tell the rest of it too!

816
00:31:35,854 --> 00:31:38,094
(Guests’ murmuring)

817
00:31:40,863 --> 00:31:42,315
It was very good! Thank you, very much!

818
00:31:43,001 --> 00:31:44,187
Goodbye! - Thank you very much

819
00:31:44,212 --> 00:31:45,894
So glad you came, Honorable Sardar! Thank you!

820
00:31:45,919 --> 00:31:46,785
Goodbye!

821
00:31:46,810 --> 00:31:47,649
Goodbye Asdollah!

822
00:31:47,674 --> 00:31:48,649
Thank you very much... please.

823
00:31:48,833 --> 00:31:49,819
Good night! Please!

824
00:31:51,336 --> 00:31:53,069
Goodbye, Khan Dadash! Goodbye, dear brother

825
00:31:53,094 --> 00:31:53,986
Goodbye to you. Goodbye!

826
00:31:54,011 --> 00:31:54,789
With your permission, goodbye!

827
00:31:54,814 --> 00:31:55,780
Take care, my dear!

828
00:31:55,805 --> 00:31:56,433
Take care!

829
00:31:57,903 --> 00:31:59,125
Well, Khan Dadash. Excuse me!

830
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:00,159
Don’t be upset!

831
00:32:00,159 --> 00:32:02,431
God willing, next time we’ll go on pilgrimage together. - God keep you. Thank you!

832
00:32:02,456 --> 00:32:03,779
Thanks so much! - Goodbye Dear Uncle!

833
00:32:04,279 --> 00:32:05,001
Sorry for the trouble.

834
00:32:05,026 --> 00:32:05,701
Goodbye.

835
00:32:05,738 --> 00:32:06,793
God keep you.

836
00:32:06,880 --> 00:32:07,776
Come on, Saeid!

837
00:32:07,958 --> 00:32:10,089
I put Dustali-Khan right in his place!

838
00:32:13,039 --> 00:32:14,655
Leili dear, you go to bed now too!

839
00:32:14,680 --> 00:32:15,432
I’m busy!

840
00:32:15,457 --> 00:32:16,185
Yes, Daddy.

841
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:18,300
Go on, my dear.

842
00:32:33,822 --> 00:32:36,008
Did you write the letter as I said?

843
00:32:36,033 --> 00:32:38,042
Exactly as you had said!

844
00:32:38,146 --> 00:32:40,012
Please act as soon as possible!

845
00:32:40,043 --> 00:32:42,071
My situation is very dangerous!

846
00:32:42,252 --> 00:32:43,548
First thing tomorrow,

847
00:32:43,572 --> 00:32:45,779
your message will go to Berlin. - Sir!

848
00:32:45,932 --> 00:32:46,811
Sir!

849
00:32:46,964 --> 00:32:47,992
Come look,

850
00:32:48,017 --> 00:32:49,151
this bastard,

851
00:32:49,176 --> 00:32:51,009
look what he’s doing!

852
00:32:51,034 --> 00:32:52,284
Who, Qasem?

853
00:32:52,465 --> 00:32:54,195
That Indian Sardar!

854
00:32:54,220 --> 00:32:55,318
Come look!

855
00:32:55,342 --> 00:32:57,610
He’s peeing on your rosebush!

856
00:32:57,635 --> 00:32:59,100
On my rosebush!

857
00:32:59,125 --> 00:32:59,624
Yes Sir!

858
00:32:59,649 --> 00:33:00,304
You saw it with your own eyes?

859
00:33:00,329 --> 00:33:01,456
Yes! We’ll go kill him!

860
00:33:01,481 --> 00:33:02,036
What?

861
00:33:02,319 --> 00:33:03,290
You want to kill him?

862
00:33:03,713 --> 00:33:04,295
Sir!

863
00:33:10,278 --> 00:33:11,353
Spy!

864
00:33:11,569 --> 00:33:12,471
Do you see?

865
00:33:12,757 --> 00:33:14,255
The English from all sides,

866
00:33:14,280 --> 00:33:15,861
want to harm me!

867
00:33:16,080 --> 00:33:19,075
This is part of their plans too!

868
00:33:19,100 --> 00:33:22,141
They want to ruin my spirit!

869
00:33:22,262 --> 00:33:24,990
They want to break my nerves with this

870
00:33:25,102 --> 00:33:27,279
so I’ll surrender to them, hands tied!

871
00:33:27,304 --> 00:33:28,096
Sir!

872
00:33:28,120 --> 00:33:30,537
In real war they were no match for me.

873
00:33:30,699 --> 00:33:33,649
Now they want to start a war of nerves.

874
00:33:33,847 --> 00:33:36,500
I’ll kill this Indian with my own hands.

875
00:33:36,525 --> 00:33:37,046
Sir!

876
00:33:38,252 --> 00:33:38,780
Keep calm!

877
00:33:38,816 --> 00:33:40,518
Don’t give the English an excuse!

878
00:33:40,752 --> 00:33:42,892
On my rosebush!

879
00:33:43,067 --> 00:33:47,658
They fight me dishonorably!

880
00:33:51,944 --> 00:33:52,932
Even,

881
00:33:53,091 --> 00:33:57,015
even if I die under English torture,

882
00:33:57,621 --> 00:34:00,824
I must make this Indian pay for what he did.

883
00:34:00,849 --> 00:34:02,218
Sir, be calm.

884
00:34:02,369 --> 00:34:03,336
Have patience.

885
00:34:03,873 --> 00:34:05,150
When the Germans arrive,

886
00:34:05,174 --> 00:34:06,963
they’ll settle this Indian’s account too!

887
00:34:07,203 --> 00:34:08,969
With my own hands,

888
00:34:09,114 --> 00:34:11,091
I’ll hang him in the garden!

889
00:34:11,182 --> 00:34:12,795
Dishonorable spy!

890
00:34:12,956 --> 00:34:13,992
Scoundrel!

891
00:34:15,282 --> 00:34:17,282
(He laughs)

892
00:34:22,362 --> 00:34:23,345
(Sound of knocking the door)

893
00:34:23,369 --> 00:34:24,296
Who is it?

894
00:34:26,239 --> 00:34:27,133
Who is it?

895
00:34:28,988 --> 00:34:30,334
Wait!

896
00:34:33,009 --> 00:34:33,617
Hello Sir!

897
00:34:33,768 --> 00:34:34,290
Naneh Joon!

898
00:34:34,449 --> 00:34:35,443
Where is Uncle Asdollah?

899
00:34:35,468 --> 00:34:35,935
In the yard.

900
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:36,927
He’s drinking tea.

901
00:34:39,639 --> 00:34:40,468
Hello, Uncle Asdollah!

902
00:34:41,634 --> 00:34:42,838
I came to inform you.

903
00:34:43,239 --> 00:34:44,428
Things have gotten really mixed up.

904
00:34:44,453 --> 00:34:46,561
Moment! Moment!

905
00:34:46,586 --> 00:34:47,633
First sit and have breakfast.

906
00:34:47,658 --> 00:34:48,417
No, thanks.

907
00:34:49,479 --> 00:34:50,276
Why not?

908
00:34:50,734 --> 00:34:51,723
I have no appetite.

909
00:34:52,405 --> 00:34:54,411
Has love for Leili killed your appetite?!

910
00:34:54,526 --> 00:34:55,219
No, Uncle!

911
00:34:55,243 --> 00:34:55,886
I’m confused.

912
00:34:55,910 --> 00:34:56,548
However much I think

913
00:34:56,573 --> 00:34:58,348
about what plan Agha Joon has in mind,

914
00:34:58,373 --> 00:34:59,374
I can’t figure it out!

915
00:34:59,613 --> 00:35:01,433
You don’t need to figure it out.

916
00:35:02,620 --> 00:35:03,553
Tell me what happened!

917
00:35:03,793 --> 00:35:04,972
Last night at the party, someone came

918
00:35:05,125 --> 00:35:06,059
for Agha Joon.

919
00:35:06,273 --> 00:35:08,245
I managed to tag along with him.

920
00:35:08,552 --> 00:35:11,024
I went to Agha Seyed Abolghasem Vaez’s house!

921
00:35:11,067 --> 00:35:12,308
Dear Uncle, out of fear of the English army,

922
00:35:12,332 --> 00:35:13,307
had hidden there.

923
00:35:13,579 --> 00:35:14,560
I never expected

924
00:35:14,584 --> 00:35:15,872
to see Dear Uncle there.

925
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:18,720
In the Constitutional era, anyone who wanted to hide

926
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:20,223
went to the English embassy

927
00:35:20,460 --> 00:35:21,547
and took sanctuary there!

928
00:35:22,140 --> 00:35:22,820
Well, go on!

929
00:35:23,398 --> 00:35:25,042
Agha Joon somehow

930
00:35:25,413 --> 00:35:26,643
got Dear Uncle

931
00:35:26,667 --> 00:35:27,995
to write a letter to Hitler

932
00:35:28,020 --> 00:35:29,416
for the Germans to come help him.

933
00:35:29,726 --> 00:35:31,856
The same letter he gave Agha Joon at the party.

934
00:35:32,700 --> 00:35:34,319
I can’t figure it out either.

935
00:35:35,233 --> 00:35:36,107
I don’t know what your father

936
00:35:36,131 --> 00:35:38,493
is plotting for this old Napoleon!

937
00:35:39,593 --> 00:35:41,833
Of course, between us, he’s a little bit right too!

938
00:35:42,627 --> 00:35:43,942
When your father had the drugstore,

939
00:35:43,966 --> 00:35:44,940
he was a wealthy man.

940
00:35:45,206 --> 00:35:46,297
Ever since your Dear Uncle

941
00:35:46,327 --> 00:35:48,348
got people to boycott his drugstore,

942
00:35:48,412 --> 00:35:51,007
he’s been as broke as us government clerks.

943
00:35:52,746 --> 00:35:53,272
Your Dear Uncle,

944
00:35:53,297 --> 00:35:54,680
took an axe to your Agha Joon’s livelihood...

945
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:55,339
And your Agha Joon too,

946
00:35:55,363 --> 00:35:55,959
has picked up the axe

947
00:35:55,983 --> 00:35:57,639
and wants to bring it down on your Dear Uncle!

948
00:35:58,074 --> 00:35:59,107
Tit for tat!

949
00:36:00,389 --> 00:36:02,305
If you, this one’s son,

950
00:36:02,330 --> 00:36:04,219
weren’t in love with that one’s daughter,

951
00:36:04,244 --> 00:36:05,788
I’d let them go at each other,

952
00:36:05,813 --> 00:36:07,096
and we’d have a good laugh!

953
00:36:07,216 --> 00:36:09,322
Today Agha Joon was in high spirits.

954
00:36:09,620 --> 00:36:11,417
I think he has a nasty plan for Dear Uncle!

955
00:36:11,448 --> 00:36:12,372
Moment!

956
00:36:12,661 --> 00:36:13,256
Your Agha Joon,

957
00:36:13,281 --> 00:36:13,996
is not the kind of man

958
00:36:14,020 --> 00:36:15,454
to send such a letter to Hitler,

959
00:36:15,479 --> 00:36:16,762
or show it to anyone.

960
00:36:16,862 --> 00:36:18,317
Then why did he make Dear Uncle

961
00:36:18,341 --> 00:36:19,710
write that letter?

962
00:36:20,160 --> 00:36:20,846
I think he wants

963
00:36:20,871 --> 00:36:22,640
something ridiculous to hold over him,

964
00:36:22,665 --> 00:36:24,230
so he can make him dance to his tune.

965
00:36:24,342 --> 00:36:25,235
To make a fool of him!

966
00:36:25,528 --> 00:36:27,832
They agreed on a code between them.

967
00:36:28,126 --> 00:36:29,231
A code?

968
00:36:29,336 --> 00:36:29,858
Yes!

969
00:36:29,882 --> 00:36:31,040
So Dear Uncle could use it

970
00:36:31,089 --> 00:36:32,444
to recognize Hitler’s agents,

971
00:36:32,468 --> 00:36:33,655
so the English spies

972
00:36:33,680 --> 00:36:34,838
can’t pull a fast one on him!

973
00:36:36,520 --> 00:36:38,050
What was that code?

974
00:36:38,559 --> 00:36:39,037
Well,

975
00:36:39,061 --> 00:36:40,357
the late Great Sir,

976
00:36:40,569 --> 00:36:43,175
with Marlene Dietrich, eats bozbash stew.

977
00:36:43,463 --> 00:36:45,032
(He guffaws)

978
00:36:45,787 --> 00:36:47,764
When Dear Uncle heard the late Great Sir’s name,

979
00:36:47,789 --> 00:36:48,742
he nearly had a stroke!

980
00:36:48,866 --> 00:36:50,353
But Agha Joon forced him to accept it.

981
00:36:51,033 --> 00:36:53,025
Your father has a sense of humor, too.

982
00:36:53,050 --> 00:36:54,027
Bravo!

983
00:36:54,211 --> 00:36:56,030
They’ve rubbed the late Great Sir

984
00:36:56,094 --> 00:36:57,115
in his face so often

985
00:36:57,302 --> 00:36:58,695
so now he’s had his revenge.

986
00:37:00,576 --> 00:37:02,185
But it’s very strange that your Dear Uncle

987
00:37:02,276 --> 00:37:03,311
went along with it.

988
00:37:03,336 --> 00:37:04,591
Agha Joon scared Dear Uncle so badly

989
00:37:04,615 --> 00:37:05,137
that he agreed

990
00:37:05,162 --> 00:37:06,263
to have the late Great Sir

991
00:37:06,430 --> 00:37:08,518
eat bozbash stew with Marlene Dietrich.

992
00:37:09,504 --> 00:37:10,880
This honorable family,

993
00:37:10,905 --> 00:37:13,352
always talks about the late Great Sir

994
00:37:13,383 --> 00:37:14,560
as if he were Victor Hugo.

995
00:37:14,629 --> 00:37:16,244
Do you even know

996
00:37:16,269 --> 00:37:16,793
who the late Great Sir was?

997
00:37:17,620 --> 00:37:18,803
No Uncle Asdollah!

998
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:21,163
But I’ve heard his name a lot.

999
00:37:21,363 --> 00:37:22,737
Then wait till I tell you.

1000
00:37:28,447 --> 00:37:30,200
The father of the late Great Sir,

1001
00:37:30,278 --> 00:37:31,576
whose soul this family

1002
00:37:31,600 --> 00:37:33,509
swears by so much,

1003
00:37:33,805 --> 00:37:36,493
under Mammad Shah or Naser al-Din Shah, I forget,

1004
00:37:36,518 --> 00:37:37,768
was the royal master builder.

1005
00:37:38,417 --> 00:37:41,392
He made a nice living off people’s bricks and mortar.

1006
00:37:41,800 --> 00:37:43,895
One day, 500 tumans, a fortune then,

1007
00:37:44,139 --> 00:37:46,128
on a silver tray, he sends to the Shah.

1008
00:37:49,646 --> 00:37:50,853
In those days, the court’s expenses

1009
00:37:50,877 --> 00:37:52,455
were paid this way.

1010
00:37:53,452 --> 00:37:56,103
The Shah gives him a seven-syllable title

1011
00:37:56,745 --> 00:37:58,811
and suddenly the master builder becomes

1012
00:37:58,836 --> 00:38:00,495
Estesqa-Saltaneh!

1013
00:38:00,825 --> 00:38:03,110
His son, that is the late Great Sir,

1014
00:38:03,341 --> 00:38:04,873
who’d carried the money on the silver tray

1015
00:38:04,897 --> 00:38:06,264
to the Shah,

1016
00:38:06,640 --> 00:38:08,161
gets a six-syllable title,

1017
00:38:08,185 --> 00:38:09,990
and becomes Estefsar-ol-Molk.

1018
00:38:10,665 --> 00:38:13,527
I don’t know why they didn’t use a gold tray!

1019
00:38:17,240 --> 00:38:19,859
The titles the notables got back then

1020
00:38:20,416 --> 00:38:21,793
depended a lot

1021
00:38:21,829 --> 00:38:23,907
on the kind of tray, whether gold

1022
00:38:24,220 --> 00:38:24,938
or silver.

1023
00:38:25,926 --> 00:38:26,942
In any case...

1024
00:38:27,204 --> 00:38:28,435
The master builder’s family

1025
00:38:28,460 --> 00:38:31,480
one day becomes part of the country’s aristocracy.

1026
00:38:32,448 --> 00:38:34,845
His son becomes Palang-Saltaneh, the “Leopard”.

1027
00:38:35,013 --> 00:38:37,042
Leopard’s son becomes Babr-ol-Molk, the “Tiger”.

1028
00:38:37,479 --> 00:38:39,940
Tiger’s son becomes Shir-od-Dowleh, the “Lion”.

1029
00:38:39,965 --> 00:38:41,987
Until it’s your Dear Uncle’s turn, and...

1030
00:38:42,011 --> 00:38:44,099
from the pain of having no title,

1031
00:38:44,599 --> 00:38:47,267
he imagines he’s Napoleon Bonaparte!

1032
00:38:51,536 --> 00:38:52,228
In short...

1033
00:38:52,252 --> 00:38:53,742
Things got to where these people

1034
00:38:53,767 --> 00:38:55,802
think no one in the world is good enough!

1035
00:38:57,160 --> 00:38:57,823
Uncle Asdollah!

1036
00:38:57,847 --> 00:38:58,515
God forbid...

1037
00:38:58,820 --> 00:39:00,664
you repeat this to anyone!

1038
00:39:02,150 --> 00:39:02,896
No!

1039
00:39:03,216 --> 00:39:04,632
Don’t worry!

1040
00:39:05,593 --> 00:39:06,251
Come up.

1041
00:39:15,440 --> 00:39:15,794
Well...

1042
00:39:15,818 --> 00:39:17,928
Now we must think of something

1043
00:39:17,952 --> 00:39:19,802
so that, God forbid, Hitler

1044
00:39:19,827 --> 00:39:21,079
doesn’t send Marshal Goering

1045
00:39:21,079 --> 00:39:23,928
to the door of a retired Cossack lieutenant!

1046
00:39:24,720 --> 00:39:25,743
Do you even know how this feud

1047
00:39:25,767 --> 00:39:26,940
between Dear Uncle and your Agha Joon,

1048
00:39:26,965 --> 00:39:28,150
got started?

1049
00:39:28,280 --> 00:39:29,188
No, I don’t know.

1050
00:39:29,436 --> 00:39:30,376
You were very little.

1051
00:39:31,145 --> 00:39:32,020
Back then,

1052
00:39:32,852 --> 00:39:35,811
your Dear Uncle was a third lieutenant of the Cossacks.

1053
00:39:35,953 --> 00:39:37,769
He showed off so much to your father

1054
00:39:38,079 --> 00:39:38,452
that your father

1055
00:39:38,477 --> 00:39:39,916
rented the same house he’s now rented out

1056
00:39:39,940 --> 00:39:41,345
to Sardar Maharat-Khan,

1057
00:39:41,732 --> 00:39:43,762
to a young second lieutenant!

1058
00:39:44,400 --> 00:39:45,061
And your Dear Uncle,

1059
00:39:45,085 --> 00:39:45,948
who at home always

1060
00:39:45,972 --> 00:39:47,664
dressed himself up like Napoleon,

1061
00:39:47,759 --> 00:39:48,591
every time he ran into

1062
00:39:48,615 --> 00:39:49,615
that young second lieutenant

1063
00:39:49,639 --> 00:39:51,222
in the alley, young enough to be his grandson,

1064
00:39:51,709 --> 00:39:53,861
he had to click his heels and salute!

1065
00:39:54,792 --> 00:39:57,516
Back then, military discipline was no joke!

1066
00:39:58,551 --> 00:40:00,268
Everyone laughed at this so much

1067
00:40:00,292 --> 00:40:02,456
that your Dear Uncle asked to retire!

1068
00:40:02,858 --> 00:40:04,028
The feud between him and your father

1069
00:40:04,052 --> 00:40:05,652
started right then.

1070
00:40:06,439 --> 00:40:07,980
But now that we

1071
00:40:08,312 --> 00:40:10,207
know the code Hitler’s agents

1072
00:40:10,231 --> 00:40:12,002
will use with your Dear Uncle,

1073
00:40:12,595 --> 00:40:14,409
we must contact him in their place,

1074
00:40:14,514 --> 00:40:16,681
so we can foil your Agha Joon’s plans!

1075
00:40:17,119 --> 00:40:18,878
How do you plan to contact him?

1076
00:40:19,840 --> 00:40:20,597
By telephone!

1077
00:40:23,145 --> 00:40:25,145
(Sound of the hand-crank telephone bell)

1078
00:40:29,583 --> 00:40:30,170
Center!

1079
00:40:30,446 --> 00:40:32,447
(Sound of the telephone ringing)

1080
00:40:45,226 --> 00:40:45,869
Yes!

1081
00:40:46,437 --> 00:40:47,039
Sir!

1082
00:40:47,849 --> 00:40:49,326
You alone is? (He speaks with changed voice and accent)

1083
00:40:49,804 --> 00:40:51,137
Then attention pay!

1084
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:53,387
The late Great Sir,

1085
00:40:53,484 --> 00:40:56,172
with Marlene Dietrich, you eat bozbash stew!

1086
00:40:56,695 --> 00:40:57,712
Understood did?

1087
00:40:58,330 --> 00:40:59,157
Yes yes!

1088
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:03,177
I’m listening.

1089
00:41:03,299 --> 00:41:05,266
You rest assured,

1090
00:41:05,700 --> 00:41:07,255
necessary order came.

1091
00:41:07,971 --> 00:41:10,215
We tomorrow with you contact took.

1092
00:41:10,487 --> 00:41:11,861
Whoever says whatever,

1093
00:41:11,885 --> 00:41:13,175
you not listen!

1094
00:41:13,447 --> 00:41:15,243
You wait for order from Berlin!

1095
00:41:15,322 --> 00:41:17,829
Even if your sister’s husband something said,

1096
00:41:17,854 --> 00:41:19,044
you not listen!

1097
00:41:19,832 --> 00:41:21,292
Completely confidential!

1098
00:41:21,972 --> 00:41:24,158
You nothing do!

1099
00:41:24,659 --> 00:41:25,846
You just wait!

1100
00:41:26,218 --> 00:41:27,148
Bravo!

1101
00:41:28,066 --> 00:41:29,536
This correct is!

1102
00:41:30,105 --> 00:41:30,545
Ja!

1103
00:41:31,198 --> 00:41:31,698
Ja, Ja!

1104
00:41:32,176 --> 00:41:32,856
Jawohl!

1105
00:41:33,879 --> 00:41:35,459
You with no one talk!

1106
00:41:35,784 --> 00:41:37,124
Until we order gave!

1107
00:41:37,680 --> 00:41:38,636
Understanding did?

1108
00:41:39,816 --> 00:41:41,597
You word of honor gave?

1109
00:41:41,837 --> 00:41:42,277
Ja!

1110
00:41:43,131 --> 00:41:43,736
Yes!

1111
00:41:43,894 --> 00:41:44,548
Yes!

1112
00:41:44,761 --> 00:41:45,416
Bravo!

1113
00:41:45,783 --> 00:41:46,730
Heil Hitler!

1114
00:41:47,576 --> 00:41:49,206
(They laugh)

1115
00:41:49,637 --> 00:41:51,550
The poor old man was trembling!

1116
00:41:51,726 --> 00:41:53,183
Now if your Agha Joon tries any mischief,

1117
00:41:53,208 --> 00:41:54,042
your Dear Uncle won’t go along with it.

1118
00:41:54,067 --> 00:41:55,282
Are you sure Agha Joon

1119
00:41:55,307 --> 00:41:57,069
won’t send that letter to Hitler?

1120
00:41:57,094 --> 00:41:58,423
Not unless he’s lost his mind!

1121
00:41:58,454 --> 00:41:59,223
And suppose

1122
00:41:59,247 --> 00:42:00,389
he sends this letter to Hitler himself,

1123
00:42:00,413 --> 00:42:01,260
or Churchill.

1124
00:42:01,285 --> 00:42:03,287
At worst: one more madman in the world!

1125
00:42:03,572 --> 00:42:05,677
If they’re in a good mood, they’ll have a good laugh.

1126
00:42:05,833 --> 00:42:06,159
In any case,

1127
00:42:06,183 --> 00:42:06,905
if you get the chance,

1128
00:42:06,929 --> 00:42:08,194
swipe this letter somehow.

1129
00:42:08,518 --> 00:42:09,610
But before you tear it,

1130
00:42:09,749 --> 00:42:10,798
bring it so we can read it together

1131
00:42:10,823 --> 00:42:11,520
and have a little laugh

1132
00:42:12,269 --> 00:42:13,591
on Hitler’s behalf.

1133
00:42:13,820 --> 00:42:14,599
But Uncle Asdollah,

1134
00:42:14,623 --> 00:42:15,675
I have a bad feeling!

1135
00:42:15,806 --> 00:42:17,760
Agha Joon has a nasty plan for this letter.

1136
00:42:18,699 --> 00:42:19,593
Honestly, what can I say!

1137
00:42:20,495 --> 00:42:21,197
Uncle Asdollah?

1138
00:42:21,297 --> 00:42:22,366
We must think of something fast,

1139
00:42:22,390 --> 00:42:23,550
before something happens.

1140
00:42:25,655 --> 00:42:26,878
Maybe you’re right.

1141
00:42:27,969 --> 00:42:29,570
Do you know where the real danger is?

1142
00:42:29,800 --> 00:42:30,989
The danger is that

1143
00:42:31,014 --> 00:42:32,000
this poor old man,

1144
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:33,765
because of your father’s jokes,

1145
00:42:34,389 --> 00:42:36,375
will go mad from fear of English revenge!

1146
00:42:36,755 --> 00:42:37,599
If I’m not wrong,

1147
00:42:37,599 --> 00:42:39,043
that’s exactly your father’s plan!

1148
00:42:50,038 --> 00:42:51,053
By the way, before I forget,

1149
00:42:51,083 --> 00:42:52,467
I’ve got news for you.

1150
00:42:52,492 --> 00:42:53,664
I think any day now

1151
00:42:53,689 --> 00:42:55,580
the Iranian army will be disbanded!

1152
00:42:55,683 --> 00:42:56,409
What does it mean?

1153
00:42:56,996 --> 00:42:59,049
It means anyone now doing military service

1154
00:42:59,074 --> 00:43:00,026
will be discharged.

1155
00:43:00,051 --> 00:43:01,077
Which means it’s quite possible

1156
00:43:01,102 --> 00:43:02,919
Poori Feshfeshoo will be back any day now!

1157
00:43:03,576 --> 00:43:04,838
Really, Uncle Asdollah?

1158
00:43:05,357 --> 00:43:06,275
Now don’t go into mourning!

1159
00:43:06,300 --> 00:43:07,737
It’ll work out somehow.

1160
00:43:08,428 --> 00:43:10,216
You need to sort out your love for Leili

1161
00:43:10,241 --> 00:43:10,970
once and for all,

1162
00:43:10,995 --> 00:43:12,611
and go to San Francisco with her.

1163
00:43:13,112 --> 00:43:14,505
But Uncle Asdollah!

1164
00:43:14,684 --> 00:43:16,033
You’re growing up now!

1165
00:43:16,057 --> 00:43:17,243
You need to know some things!

1166
00:43:18,258 --> 00:43:19,311
With women, it’s the first look:

1167
00:43:19,335 --> 00:43:20,504
you’ve got them, or not.

1168
00:43:20,656 --> 00:43:22,690
If not, don’t keep chasing!

1169
00:43:23,126 --> 00:43:25,685
Leili is the kind who’ll come to you on her own.

1170
00:43:25,710 --> 00:43:27,467
I must give you a few lessons!

1171
00:43:28,100 --> 00:43:29,603
For now listen to your first lesson.

1172
00:43:30,353 --> 00:43:31,521
When you meet women,

1173
00:43:31,545 --> 00:43:33,567
show them you’re a customer.

1174
00:43:33,765 --> 00:43:34,878
Shopping for goods!

1175
00:43:35,018 --> 00:43:35,920
A buyer.

1176
00:43:36,355 --> 00:43:36,852
Then,

1177
00:43:36,876 --> 00:43:38,796
go to sleep with peace of mind.

1178
00:43:38,898 --> 00:43:41,012
You’ve booked your San Francisco ticket.

1179
00:43:41,333 --> 00:43:42,202
They’ll come to you themselves

1180
00:43:42,226 --> 00:43:43,635
so you can go to San Francisco together.

1181
00:43:44,073 --> 00:43:44,777
Uncle Asdollah, I...

1182
00:43:44,802 --> 00:43:46,359
Uncle Asdollah, my foot!

1183
00:43:47,370 --> 00:43:48,111
You’ll tell me again

1184
00:43:48,135 --> 00:43:50,229
your heart beats for a heavenly love?

1185
00:43:50,348 --> 00:43:51,335
Well, let it beat!

1186
00:43:51,964 --> 00:43:53,126
Keep talking this nonsense

1187
00:43:53,151 --> 00:43:53,792
until they marry the girl off,

1188
00:43:53,817 --> 00:43:55,152
then sit around sighing over her memory!

1189
00:43:55,192 --> 00:43:56,666
Isn’t that how love should be?

1190
00:43:56,691 --> 00:43:58,778
Then what about all the things they write in books?

1191
00:43:58,883 --> 00:43:59,559
Moment!

1192
00:43:59,584 --> 00:44:01,004
Really Moment!

1193
00:44:01,028 --> 00:44:02,883
As tall as you are, you still don’t know a thing!

1194
00:44:02,908 --> 00:44:04,196
Which books?

1195
00:44:04,578 --> 00:44:06,684
The book is what I’m teaching you!

1196
00:44:06,935 --> 00:44:07,801
Second lesson!

1197
00:44:08,224 --> 00:44:10,010
Always give the other side an excuse

1198
00:44:10,035 --> 00:44:11,765
so she can use it to come to you!

1199
00:44:11,987 --> 00:44:13,322
Well, what if she doesn’t come? Moment!

1200
00:44:14,113 --> 00:44:16,191
You have to play it so she doesn’t notice.

1201
00:44:18,096 --> 00:44:20,116
Shall I give you lesson three too? Or is that too much?

1202
00:44:20,719 --> 00:44:21,944
Uncle Asdollah!

1203
00:44:22,341 --> 00:44:23,370
Lesson three is:

1204
00:44:23,394 --> 00:44:24,174
never, ever

1205
00:44:24,198 --> 00:44:26,247
put on such a goody-goody face.

1206
00:44:26,272 --> 00:44:27,280
As soon as women see

1207
00:44:27,305 --> 00:44:29,325
you’ve got a meek, goody-goody face,

1208
00:44:29,577 --> 00:44:31,388
even if you sing like Qamar-ol-Moluk Vaziri,

1209
00:44:31,412 --> 00:44:33,127
they’ll say: Ugh! What a cold voice!

1210
00:44:33,318 --> 00:44:34,702
If you’re Clark Gable, they’ll say:

1211
00:44:34,727 --> 00:44:36,666
Ugh! Handsome, but so dull!

1212
00:44:37,761 --> 00:44:39,055
Looks like you’re not listening.

1213
00:44:39,086 --> 00:44:40,187
All right, the rest can wait.

1214
00:44:40,323 --> 00:44:41,426
It’s all I think about!

1215
00:44:41,511 --> 00:44:43,657
I’m afraid this Hitler and Germans business

1216
00:44:43,864 --> 00:44:45,246
will set Dear Uncle and Agha Joon

1217
00:44:45,297 --> 00:44:47,006
at each other’s throats again!

1218
00:44:47,167 --> 00:44:49,129
And you’ll lose your dear Leili?

1219
00:44:49,462 --> 00:44:50,835
Take it from me,

1220
00:44:50,859 --> 00:44:53,072
with that look and those innocent eyes of yours,

1221
00:44:53,097 --> 00:44:55,247
you’ll certainly lose Leili.

1222
00:44:55,710 --> 00:44:57,651
Then you’ll be left sighing over her. - But...

1223
00:44:58,226 --> 00:44:59,773
Then what do you say I should do?

1224
00:45:01,319 --> 00:45:02,583
San Francisco!

1225
00:45:02,834 --> 00:45:03,591
Uncle Asdollah!

1226
00:45:03,615 --> 00:45:04,400
Please,

1227
00:45:04,425 --> 00:45:06,162
don’t talk like that... - If you don’t want to go to San Francisco,

1228
00:45:06,187 --> 00:45:07,643
at least visit the suburbs!

1229
00:45:07,668 --> 00:45:08,810
The outskirts!

1230
00:45:09,333 --> 00:45:12,007
Show at least you’re the traveling type!

1231
00:45:18,714 --> 00:45:19,734
Moment!

1232
00:45:20,720 --> 00:45:22,519
I’ve thought of a way!

1233
00:45:27,729 --> 00:45:29,370
It may not be a bad way!

1234
00:45:29,745 --> 00:45:31,740
Looks like I’ll skip out of the office again today!

1235
00:45:31,771 --> 00:45:32,554
Come on! - But why?

1236
00:45:32,801 --> 00:45:33,968
I’ll tell you later!

1237
00:45:34,520 --> 00:45:35,410
Yes, sir! - Here, take this!

1238
00:45:35,942 --> 00:45:36,776
God bless you.

1239
00:45:37,012 --> 00:45:38,489
Now you run along home!

1240
00:45:38,617 --> 00:45:39,752
If you can somehow,

1241
00:45:39,984 --> 00:45:41,508
that letter your Dear Uncle Napoleon

1242
00:45:41,532 --> 00:45:42,752
wrote to Hitler,

1243
00:45:43,152 --> 00:45:43,698
swipe it!

1244
00:45:43,819 --> 00:45:44,568
I don’t think I can!

1245
00:45:44,592 --> 00:45:46,208
I guess Agha Joon has put it in his desk drawer,

1246
00:45:46,232 --> 00:45:48,207
and locked it! - I said if you can!

1247
00:45:49,512 --> 00:45:50,930
Go, I’ll see you tonight! - Goodbye. Get going.

1248
00:45:55,640 --> 00:45:58,460
(Sound of children’s play)

1249
00:46:00,340 --> 00:46:03,226
- We have a ferris wheel...

1250
00:46:03,359 --> 00:46:07,434
O granter of needs.

1251
00:46:09,526 --> 00:46:10,675
Why are you sitting here?

1252
00:46:10,699 --> 00:46:11,694
In everyone’s way!

1253
00:46:12,129 --> 00:46:13,071
What else can I do, Sir!

1254
00:46:14,149 --> 00:46:15,346
Are you new around here?

1255
00:46:16,359 --> 00:46:18,576
Yes, sir! It’s been a few days!

1256
00:46:20,440 --> 00:46:22,048
How’s business?

1257
00:46:22,568 --> 00:46:23,785
Not great!

1258
00:46:24,741 --> 00:46:26,228
Why don’t you go to Tree Alley?

1259
00:46:26,867 --> 00:46:27,734
The alley over there?

1260
00:46:28,640 --> 00:46:29,454
Well, Sir...

1261
00:46:29,478 --> 00:46:31,034
God provides a man’s daily bread!

1262
00:46:31,058 --> 00:46:32,435
Here or there, it’s all the same!

1263
00:46:32,460 --> 00:46:33,315
Moment!

1264
00:46:33,339 --> 00:46:34,759
What nonsense!

1265
00:46:35,053 --> 00:46:37,001
What do you mean, no difference?

1266
00:46:37,652 --> 00:46:39,279
If you come into Tree Alley,

1267
00:46:39,310 --> 00:46:41,974
I get my shoes shined twice a day!

1268
00:46:42,686 --> 00:46:44,321
And all our neighbors, too,

1269
00:46:44,345 --> 00:46:45,238
to find

1270
00:46:45,262 --> 00:46:47,737
a cobbler or shoe-shiner, have to walk a long way,

1271
00:46:47,780 --> 00:46:49,145
to the other side of the street!

1272
00:46:49,266 --> 00:46:50,051
It’s an upscale alley!

1273
00:46:50,461 --> 00:46:51,978
Who’d get a shine here?

1274
00:46:52,054 --> 00:46:53,216
People won’t let me, Sir!

1275
00:46:53,687 --> 00:46:55,253
As soon as you set up somewhere,

1276
00:46:55,277 --> 00:46:56,668
they come right away: pack it up!

1277
00:46:56,692 --> 00:46:57,290
Saying what?

1278
00:46:57,341 --> 00:46:58,236
You’re sitting at our door!

1279
00:46:59,100 --> 00:47:00,576
To hell with them!

1280
00:47:00,646 --> 00:47:02,840
Pack up your kit and come to the next alley!

1281
00:47:03,150 --> 00:47:04,112
Right at my door!

1282
00:47:04,528 --> 00:47:05,263
Under the tree!

1283
00:47:05,348 --> 00:47:06,181
Cool!

1284
00:47:06,326 --> 00:47:07,656
Real customers!

1285
00:47:08,219 --> 00:47:10,514
Some tip as much as the shine costs!

1286
00:47:11,080 --> 00:47:12,782
Why sit here by the road!

1287
00:47:13,499 --> 00:47:14,705
You shine them on one side,

1288
00:47:14,814 --> 00:47:16,228
and dust settles on the other!

1289
00:47:17,246 --> 00:47:18,499
Your other foot, Sir!

1290
00:47:20,599 --> 00:47:21,558
Yes my dear!

1291
00:47:26,559 --> 00:47:27,644
Will you tell everyone

1292
00:47:27,668 --> 00:47:29,037
to bring their shoes to me?

1293
00:47:29,575 --> 00:47:30,543
Of course!

1294
00:47:30,791 --> 00:47:32,960
I promise you two pairs a day myself.

1295
00:47:33,495 --> 00:47:35,381
Bread... cool water...

1296
00:47:35,978 --> 00:47:36,782
Here, if you get thirsty,

1297
00:47:36,867 --> 00:47:38,474
who’ll hand you a bowl of cool water?

1298
00:47:39,712 --> 00:47:40,598
Really, Sir?

1299
00:47:41,165 --> 00:47:42,957
Just come for a few days!

1300
00:47:43,068 --> 00:47:44,557
If you don’t like it, don’t come!

1301
00:47:45,050 --> 00:47:46,581
This alley won’t run away!

1302
00:47:47,478 --> 00:47:49,248
May God never take you from us!

1303
00:47:49,746 --> 00:47:50,814
Is tomorrow good?

1304
00:47:52,529 --> 00:47:53,504
No! Why tomorrow?

1305
00:47:53,528 --> 00:47:54,698
In an hour, when...

1306
00:47:54,777 --> 00:47:55,731
I’m there myself!

1307
00:47:55,960 --> 00:47:56,415
Look!

1308
00:47:56,625 --> 00:47:58,013
When you get there,

1309
00:47:58,037 --> 00:47:59,538
sit outside the garden gate.

1310
00:48:00,319 --> 00:48:01,600
Facing the door!

1311
00:48:02,007 --> 00:48:02,947
On the walkway!

1312
00:48:03,576 --> 00:48:04,858
It’s very airy!

1313
00:48:04,982 --> 00:48:06,653
You’ll love it when you’re tired.

1314
00:48:06,792 --> 00:48:07,586
Lovely!

1315
00:48:08,512 --> 00:48:09,659
Airy!

1316
00:48:11,405 --> 00:48:12,831
It’s no joke, kid!

1317
00:48:13,566 --> 00:48:15,788
No wonder Sir can’t sleep at night!

1318
00:48:16,209 --> 00:48:17,975
The godless English

1319
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:19,025
are coming!

1320
00:48:20,662 --> 00:48:22,476
Maybe their man’s on his way now

1321
00:48:22,501 --> 00:48:23,765
to come and, God forbid,

1322
00:48:23,789 --> 00:48:25,499
do something terrible to Sir!

1323
00:48:26,580 --> 00:48:29,394
Sir and I are nearly worried to death!

1324
00:48:29,497 --> 00:48:32,067
Last night while I stood guard at his door,

1325
00:48:32,350 --> 00:48:34,210
he woke up ten times from fear!

1326
00:48:35,914 --> 00:48:37,428
Even asleep he was shouting:

1327
00:48:37,452 --> 00:48:39,293
They’ve come! They’re here!

1328
00:48:39,760 --> 00:48:41,070
But why Mash Ghasem?

1329
00:48:41,726 --> 00:48:43,206
Honestly, kid, why lie?

1330
00:48:43,299 --> 00:48:45,094
The grave is this close!

1331
00:48:46,170 --> 00:48:47,883
It’s as if an English bullet

1332
00:48:47,908 --> 00:48:48,921
is flying through the air,

1333
00:48:48,953 --> 00:48:51,037
about to hit him right between the eyes!

1334
00:48:52,787 --> 00:48:53,571
To tell the truth, kid!

1335
00:48:53,595 --> 00:48:55,313
I’m not in great shape myself!

1336
00:48:55,985 --> 00:48:57,765
But I put my trust in God!

1337
00:48:59,152 --> 00:49:01,319
I mean, kid, the English have a point too!

1338
00:49:01,558 --> 00:49:02,775
If we were in their place

1339
00:49:02,800 --> 00:49:04,616
and someone had ruined us like this,

1340
00:49:04,641 --> 00:49:06,904
we wouldn’t let him get away alive either.

1341
00:49:07,353 --> 00:49:08,463
I don’t think the English

1342
00:49:08,487 --> 00:49:09,994
have it in for you that much!

1343
00:49:10,019 --> 00:49:11,325
You have no idea, kid!

1344
00:49:11,953 --> 00:49:15,364
The English and I are like the devil and holy water!

1345
00:49:16,774 --> 00:49:19,009
Say they’ve forgotten the Mamasani war,

1346
00:49:19,034 --> 00:49:20,224
what about the Kazerun war?

1347
00:49:20,892 --> 00:49:22,752
Say they’ve forgotten the Kazerun war,

1348
00:49:22,776 --> 00:49:24,221
what about the Ghias Abad war?

1349
00:49:25,563 --> 00:49:27,664
But I swear by this lamp’s light!

1350
00:49:27,981 --> 00:49:29,585
By my family’s honor!

1351
00:49:30,055 --> 00:49:31,083
I’d gladly let

1352
00:49:31,107 --> 00:49:33,085
the English blow me from a cannon,

1353
00:49:33,254 --> 00:49:35,165
as long as they leave Sir alone!

1354
00:49:35,652 --> 00:49:36,227
Where are you going?

1355
00:49:36,251 --> 00:49:37,387
To buy bread!

1356
00:49:37,611 --> 00:49:39,017
Photography is! (He speaks with an Armenian accent)

1357
00:49:41,480 --> 00:49:44,004
For one qeran, photo looking just like you!

1358
00:49:47,874 --> 00:49:49,993
Photography is, photography!

1359
00:49:51,608 --> 00:49:52,979
Photography is.

1360
00:49:54,211 --> 00:49:55,491
Photography.

1361
00:49:56,400 --> 00:49:57,792
As if it is the voice of Mirza Habib!

1362
00:49:58,208 --> 00:49:59,028
As if it is himself!

1363
00:49:59,260 --> 00:50:01,521
For one qeran, photo looking just like you!

1364
00:50:03,147 --> 00:50:03,866
Photography.

1365
00:50:06,136 --> 00:50:07,411
We take photo.

1366
00:50:07,961 --> 00:50:08,978
Photo.

1367
00:50:10,868 --> 00:50:12,082
Photography is.

1368
00:50:14,526 --> 00:50:15,699
Photography.

1369
00:50:19,133 --> 00:50:20,879
We take photo, photo! - Mirza Habib!

1370
00:50:21,566 --> 00:50:21,992
Come!

1371
00:50:23,023 --> 00:50:23,362
Come!

1372
00:50:31,246 --> 00:50:32,859
I am not Mirza Habib!

1373
00:50:32,932 --> 00:50:34,612
Isn’t this camera Mirza Habib’s?

1374
00:50:34,767 --> 00:50:37,137
Mirza Habib, his camera, sold to me.

1375
00:50:37,479 --> 00:50:38,734
If you want to take a photo,

1376
00:50:38,758 --> 00:50:40,329
I take prettier than him.

1377
00:50:40,945 --> 00:50:42,710
Mirza Habib was my apprentice.

1378
00:50:42,990 --> 00:50:43,632
Then come!

1379
00:50:43,829 --> 00:50:44,692
Come take a photo!

1380
00:50:44,942 --> 00:50:45,483
Yes!

1381
00:50:45,508 --> 00:50:46,065
Come in!

